1
00:01:30,715 --> 00:01:35,762
I should have known you'd be here,
Professor McGonagall.

2
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:49,233
Good evening,
Professor Dumbledore.

3
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:55,740
Are the rumors true, Albus?

4
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:59,160
I'm afraid so, Professor.
The good...

5
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:01,496
...and the bad.

6
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:04,749
- And the boy?
- Hagrid is bringing him.

7
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:08,753
Do you think it's wise to trust
Hagrid with something so important?

8
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:13,591
Professor, I would trust Hagrid
with my life.

9
00:02:33,069 --> 00:02:36,322
Professor Dumbledore, sir.
Professor McGonagall.

10
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:39,450
No problems, I hope, Hagrid?

11
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:44,831
No, sir. The baby fell asleep
as we were flying over Bristol.

12
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:48,793
Try not to wake him.

13
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:51,796
Here you are.

14
00:02:57,135 --> 00:03:02,140
Albus, do you really think it's safe
to leave him with these people?

15
00:03:02,306 --> 00:03:07,145
I've watched them all day. They're
the worst sort of Muggles imaginable.

16
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:11,190
- They really are...
- The only family he has.

17
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,860
This boy will be famous.

18
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:16,988
There won't be a child in our world
who doesn't know his name.

19
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:22,326
Exactly. He'll be better off
growing up away from all that.

20
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:28,082
Until he's ready.

21
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:44,849
There, there, Hagrid. You're not
saying goodbye forever.

22
00:03:57,862 --> 00:03:59,447
Good luck...

23
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,575
...Harry Potter.

24
00:04:08,956 --> 00:04:13,711
HARRY POTTER
AND THE SORCERER'S STONE

25
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:22,804
Up! Get up!

26
00:04:25,807 --> 00:04:27,517
Right now!

27
00:04:41,072 --> 00:04:44,408
Wake up, cousin!
We're going to the zoo!

28
00:04:55,378 --> 00:05:00,800
- Here comes the birthday boy!
- Happy birthday, son.

29
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:05,805
Why don't you make breakfast?
And try not to burn anything.

30
00:05:06,013 --> 00:05:11,102
- Yes, Aunt Petunia.
- I want everything to be perfect...

31
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:15,731
- ...on my Dudley's special day.
- Hurry up!

32
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,942
- Get my coffee, boy.
- Yes, Uncle Vernon.

33
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,613
Aren't they wonderful, darling?

34
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:28,953
- How many are there?
- Thirty-six. I counted them myself.

35
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:32,790
Thirty-six? But last year
I got thirty-seven!

36
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,293
Yes, but some are much bigger
than last year's.

37
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:38,963
- I don't care!
- Now, now. Here's what we'll do:

38
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:44,135
When we go out, we'll buy you
two more presents. All right, darling?

39
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,898
I'm warning you, boy.

40
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:00,651
You do anything strange, anything at all...

41
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:04,071
...and you won't eat for a week.

42
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:06,365
Get in.

43
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:09,577
REPTILE HOUSE

44
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,666
Make it move!

45
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:20,338
Move!

46
00:06:20,504 --> 00:06:22,673
- Move!
- She's asleep!

47
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:25,176
She's boring.

48
00:06:28,262 --> 00:06:33,684
Excuse him. He doesn't know what it's like
to lie there day after day...

49
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:37,313
...watching people press
their faces up against the glass.

50
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:43,027
Can you hear me?

51
00:06:45,821 --> 00:06:49,951
It's just that I've never
talked to a snake before.

52
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:53,120
Do you...

53
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,748
...do you talk to people often?

54
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:59,043
You're from Burma, aren't you?

55
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:02,380
Was it nice there?
Do you miss your family?

56
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,549
BRED IN CAPTIVITY

57
00:07:05,841 --> 00:07:07,426
I see.

58
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:10,721
The same thing happened to me.
I never knew my parents.

59
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:14,433
Mum! Dad! Come and see
what this snake's doing!

60
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:42,670
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

61
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:47,508
Snake!

62
00:08:03,482 --> 00:08:06,777
Mum! Mummy!
Help me, please!

63
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:10,114
My darling boy!
How did you get in there?

64
00:08:10,614 --> 00:08:15,202
Oh my God, how did you get in there?
Is there a snake?

65
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:24,795
Don't worry, darling.
We'll get those cold clothes off you.

66
00:08:27,631 --> 00:08:30,551
- What happened?
- I swear I don't know!

67
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,055
The glass was there, then it vanished!
It was like magic!

68
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:41,979
There's no such thing as magic.

69
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:03,709
MR. H. POTTER
THE CUPBOARD UNDER THE STAIRS

70
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:22,853
- Marge got sick. Bad clam.
- Dad, Harry got a letter!

71
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:24,730
Give it to me!

72
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:28,484
Who would be writing to you?

73
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:02,560
No more mail is coming
through this letterbox.

74
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,950
Have a good day at the office, dear.

75
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,664
Out of the way!

76
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:51,442
What a lovely day, Sunday.

77
00:10:52,401 --> 00:10:56,030
In my opinion, the best day
of the week. Why is that, Dudley?

78
00:10:57,406 --> 00:11:00,910
- Because there's no post?
- Exactly, Harry.

79
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:03,662
There's no post on Sundays.

80
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:10,002
No blasted letters today!
No, sir!

81
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:14,632
Not a single blasted letter. Not one!

82
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:27,853
No, sir. Not one single
miserable, blasted...

83
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:41,659
Make it stop, Mummy, please!

84
00:11:48,707 --> 00:11:52,920
- Please tell me, what's happening?
- What's this?

85
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:57,132
Give me that!

86
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:00,177
Give me that letter!

87
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,306
Let me go!

88
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:11,563
They're my letters! Let go of me!

89
00:12:13,148 --> 00:12:16,277
That's it! We're leaving!

90
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:20,698
Far away! Somewhere
they can't find us!

91
00:12:20,864 --> 00:12:23,617
Daddy's gone mad, hasn't he?

92
00:12:46,724 --> 00:12:50,060
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

93
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,863
Make a wish, Harry.

94
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,881
Who's there?

95
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,937
Sorry about that.

96
00:13:40,944 --> 00:13:44,948
I demand you leave at once.
You're trespassing!

97
00:13:48,285 --> 00:13:51,288
Oh, shut up, Dursley,
you great prune.

98
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,588
I haven't seen you since
you were a baby, Harry, but...

99
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:03,133
...I didn't expect you to be so big,
especially around the middle.

100
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:06,387
I'm not Harry.

101
00:14:09,515 --> 00:14:13,310
- I am.
- Of course, of course.

102
00:14:14,269 --> 00:14:18,315
I've brought you something.
I might've sat on it at some point...

103
00:14:18,482 --> 00:14:21,151
...but I reckon
it'll taste all right.

104
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:26,115
I baked it myself,
words and all.

105
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:32,704
HAPPEE BIRTHDAE, HARRY

106
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:35,290
- Thanks.
- It's not every day your boy...

107
00:14:35,499 --> 00:14:37,668
...turns eleven, is it?

108
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:56,186
Excuse me, but...

109
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:59,440
- ...who are you?
- Rubeus Hagrid.

110
00:14:59,648 --> 00:15:02,651
Keeper of Keys
and Grounds at Hogwarts.

111
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:06,738
- Of course you know about Hogwarts.
- Sorry, no.

112
00:15:07,322 --> 00:15:11,743
No? Blimey, haven't you ever wondered
where your parents learned it all?

113
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:15,873
- Learned what?
- You're a wizard, Harry.

114
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:20,002
- I'm a what?
- A wizard.

115
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:23,213
And a very good one, I'd wager,
once you've been trained a little.

116
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:25,924
No. You've made a mistake. I mean...

117
00:15:26,425 --> 00:15:29,428
I can't be a wizard.

118
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:32,431
I mean, I'm just...

119
00:15:32,639 --> 00:15:34,892
Harry. Just Harry.

120
00:15:35,934 --> 00:15:40,063
Well, Just Harry, haven't you ever
made anything happen?

121
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:43,692
Anything you couldn't explain
when you were angry or scared?

122
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:04,421
"Dear Mr. Potter,
we are pleased to inform you...

123
00:16:04,588 --> 00:16:07,925
...that you have been accepted at Hogwarts
School of Witchcraft and Wizardry."

124
00:16:08,091 --> 00:16:10,344
And I'm telling you he's not going.

125
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:13,055
When we took him in, we swore
we'd put a stop to all this rubbish.

126
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:14,973
You knew?

127
00:16:15,182 --> 00:16:17,559
All along, and you
never told me?

128
00:16:17,768 --> 00:16:20,854
Of course we knew.
How could you not be?

129
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:24,441
My perfect sister,
being what she was.

130
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:30,113
My parents were so proud
when she got her letter.

131
00:16:30,948 --> 00:16:34,701
"We have a witch
in the family. Isn't that wonderful?"

132
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:38,372
I was the only one
who saw her for what she was.

133
00:16:39,331 --> 00:16:41,166
A freak!

134
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,711
Then she met Potter and had you,
and I knew...

135
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:48,674
...you'd be just as strange,
just as...

136
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:53,470
...abnormal. And then, as if that
wasn't enough, she got herself blown up...

137
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:56,890
- ...and we were left with you.
- Blown up?

138
00:16:57,099 --> 00:16:59,726
You told me they died
in a car crash.

139
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:01,812
A car crash?

140
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:04,189
A car crash killed Lily
and James Potter?

141
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,817
- We had to say something.
- It's an outrage!

142
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:09,820
- It's a scandal!
- He's not going.

143
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,658
And I suppose a great Muggle
like yourself is going to stop him, eh?

144
00:17:14,825 --> 00:17:16,994
- Muggle?
- Non-magic folk.

145
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:19,538
Harry's been registered
since the day he was born.

146
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:23,375
He'll go to the finest school
of witchcraft and wizardry in the world...

147
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:27,921
...and he'll study under the finest
headmaster Hogwarts has ever seen...

148
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:30,173
...Albus Dumbledore.

149
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:34,344
I will not pay for some crackpot old fool
to teach him magic tricks!

150
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:36,555
Never...

151
00:17:36,763 --> 00:17:41,685
...insult Albus Dumbledore
in front of me.

152
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:05,000
I'd appreciate it if you didn't tell
anyone at Hogwarts what I did.

153
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:08,378
- I'm not supposed to use magic.
- All right.

154
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:13,925
Well, we're running a bit late.
Better get going.

155
00:18:20,182 --> 00:18:22,684
Unless you'd rather stay,
of course.

156
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:40,911
"All students must arrive
equipped with...

157
00:18:41,119 --> 00:18:44,206
...one standard-size-two
pewter cauldron...

158
00:18:44,414 --> 00:18:46,208
...and may bring, if they wish...

159
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:49,127
...an owl, a cat or a toad."

160
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:52,714
Do they sell all this in London?

161
00:18:53,006 --> 00:18:55,008
If you know where to go.

162
00:19:18,281 --> 00:19:21,284
Ah, Hagrid, the usual, I presume.

163
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:24,663
No, thanks, Tom. I'm here
on official Hogwarts business.

164
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:28,750
We're getting Harry
his school supplies.

165
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:32,462
Good Lord.
It's Harry Potter!

166
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:39,803
Welcome back, Mr. Potter.
Welcome.

167
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:44,683
Doris Crockford. I can't believe
I'm finally meeting you.

168
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,936
Harry Po-Potter.

169
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:50,480
I can't tell you how pleased
I am to meet you.

170
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:55,068
Hello, Professor, didn't see you there.
Harry, this is Professor Quirrell.

171
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:59,072
He'll teach you Defense
Against the Dark Arts.

172
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,074
Nice to meet you.

173
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:04,536
It's a most fa-fascinating subject.

174
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,498
Though you won't ne-need it,
will you, Potter?

175
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:14,504
Yes, well, we must be going.
Lots to buy.

176
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:16,381
Goodbye.

177
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:22,679
- See, Harry? You're famous.
- But why am I famous, Hagrid?

178
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:26,349
How do all those people
over there know who I am?

179
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:29,728
I'm not sure I'm the right person
to tell you that.

180
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,748
Welcome, Harry,
to Diagon Alley.

181
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:09,893
We'll buy your quills
and ink here.

182
00:21:10,101 --> 00:21:13,396
And over there, everything
you need for spells.

183
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:41,216
It's a great racing broom.

184
00:21:41,424 --> 00:21:44,719
Look at that!
The new Nimbus 2000!

185
00:21:45,428 --> 00:21:48,265
It's the fastest model
they've ever made.

186
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:57,107
But how am I going to pay for all this?
I haven't any money.

187
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,694
There's your money, Harry.
In Gringotts, the wizard bank.

188
00:22:00,902 --> 00:22:04,865
Safest place there is. None safer.
Except perhaps Hogwarts.

189
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,797
Hagrid...

190
00:22:21,172 --> 00:22:24,718
- ...what exactly are these things?
- They're goblins, Harry.

191
00:22:25,051 --> 00:22:28,680
Very clever, they are,
but not the friendliest of creatures.

192
00:22:28,889 --> 00:22:30,682
Stay close.

193
00:22:34,561 --> 00:22:37,814
Mr. Harry Potter
wishes to make a withdrawal.

194
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:45,822
And does Mr. Harry Potter
have his key?

195
00:22:46,823 --> 00:22:48,825
Just a moment. Got it here somewhere.

196
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,665
There it is, the little rascal.

197
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:58,043
Oh, and there's something else I need.

198
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,213
Professor Dumbledore gave me this.

199
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:07,177
TOP SECRET

200
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:11,890
It's about You-Know-What
in vault You-Know-Which.

201
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:15,518
Very well.

202
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:22,275
Vault 687.

203
00:23:25,528 --> 00:23:27,364
Lamp, please.

204
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,791
Key, please.

205
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:04,442
You didn't think your parents would
leave you with nothing, did you?

206
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:08,446
Vault 713.

207
00:24:08,655 --> 00:24:11,574
- What's in there, Hagrid?
- Can't tell you.

208
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:14,411
Hogwarts business.
Very secret.

209
00:24:14,619 --> 00:24:16,162
Stand back.

210
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:47,277
Best not mention any of this
to anyone, Harry.

211
00:24:55,618 --> 00:24:58,955
I still need... a wand.

212
00:24:59,622 --> 00:25:03,209
A wand? You need to go to Ollivanders.
No better place.

213
00:25:04,002 --> 00:25:06,046
Why don't you go and wait for me there?

214
00:25:06,254 --> 00:25:08,923
I've got one more thing to do.
Won't be long.

215
00:25:26,941 --> 00:25:28,610
Hello?

216
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:33,323
Hello?

217
00:25:36,993 --> 00:25:41,206
I wondered when I'd be seeing you,
Mr. Potter.

218
00:25:49,255 --> 00:25:51,466
It seems only yesterday...

219
00:25:51,674 --> 00:25:56,721
...your mother and father were here
buying their first wands.

220
00:26:04,020 --> 00:26:05,939
Here you are.

221
00:26:15,073 --> 00:26:17,075
Give it a wave.

222
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:26,292
Apparently not.

223
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:35,969
Perhaps...

224
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:39,764
...this one.

225
00:26:47,188 --> 00:26:50,275
No, no, definitely not.

226
00:26:50,733 --> 00:26:52,569
Never mind.

227
00:26:59,033 --> 00:27:00,618
I wonder...

228
00:27:29,939 --> 00:27:31,774
How curious.

229
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:34,861
Very curious.

230
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:38,740
Excuse me, but
what's curious?

231
00:27:40,283 --> 00:27:43,369
I remember every single
wand I've ever sold.

232
00:27:43,786 --> 00:27:46,789
It so happens that the phoenix...

233
00:27:46,956 --> 00:27:51,502
...whose tail feather is in your wand
gave another feather.

234
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:55,048
Just one other tail feather.

235
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:59,385
It's curious that this wand
should be destined for you...

236
00:27:59,761 --> 00:28:04,807
...when its brother
gave you that scar.

237
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:10,146
And who owned that wand?

238
00:28:11,439 --> 00:28:13,816
We do not speak his name.

239
00:28:14,275 --> 00:28:17,904
The wand chooses
the wizard, Mr. Potter.

240
00:28:18,112 --> 00:28:20,698
It's not always clear why...

241
00:28:21,282 --> 00:28:24,869
...but I think it is clear...

242
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:27,914
...that we can expect great things
from you.

243
00:28:29,082 --> 00:28:33,503
After all,
He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named...

244
00:28:33,711 --> 00:28:36,339
...did great things.

245
00:28:36,547 --> 00:28:38,299
Terrible...

246
00:28:39,008 --> 00:28:42,345
...yes. But great.

247
00:28:47,850 --> 00:28:49,894
Harry. Harry!

248
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:52,355
Happy birthday.

249
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,233
Wow!

250
00:28:59,821 --> 00:29:02,782
Are you all right, Harry?
You've gone very quiet.

251
00:29:03,658 --> 00:29:08,705
He killed my parents, didn't he?
The one who gave me this.

252
00:29:09,539 --> 00:29:11,291
You know, Hagrid.

253
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:14,127
I know you know.

254
00:29:16,879 --> 00:29:20,633
First, understand this, Harry,
because it's very important...

255
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:25,555
...not all wizards are good.
Some go bad.

256
00:29:25,763 --> 00:29:29,434
A few years ago, there was a wizard
who went as bad as you can go.

257
00:29:29,642 --> 00:29:31,561
And his name was V...

258
00:29:32,603 --> 00:29:34,230
His name was V...

259
00:29:34,564 --> 00:29:39,444
- Can you write it down?
- No, I can't spell it. Well...

260
00:29:40,194 --> 00:29:42,613
- Voldemort.
- Voldemort?

261
00:29:46,701 --> 00:29:48,786
Those were dark times, Harry.

262
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:54,375
<i>Voldemort began
to gather followers.</i>

263
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:57,211
<i>He brought them over to the Dark Side.</i>

264
00:29:59,255 --> 00:30:02,175
<i>Anyone who stood up to him
ended up dead.</i>

265
00:30:03,426 --> 00:30:05,470
<i>Your parents fought him.</i>

266
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:09,599
<i>But no one survived once he
decided to kill them.</i>

267
00:30:14,812 --> 00:30:19,150
<i>No one. Not a single person.
Except you.</i>

268
00:30:22,028 --> 00:30:26,282
Me? Voldemort
tried to kill me?

269
00:30:26,616 --> 00:30:30,661
Yes. That mark on your forehead
isn't an ordinary cut.

270
00:30:31,162 --> 00:30:34,374
It happened when a powerful
curse touched you...

271
00:30:34,582 --> 00:30:36,918
...an evil curse.

272
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:40,671
What happened to V...
to You-Know-Who?

273
00:30:41,672 --> 00:30:44,467
Some say he died.

274
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:47,970
Rubbish, if you ask me.

275
00:30:48,137 --> 00:30:51,516
No. I think he's still
out there somewhere.

276
00:30:51,724 --> 00:30:54,268
Too weak to carry on.

277
00:30:54,644 --> 00:31:00,108
But one thing's certain. Something
about you stopped him that night.

278
00:31:00,316 --> 00:31:04,654
That's why you're famous. That's why
everyone knows your name.

279
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:07,490
You're the boy who lived.

280
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:20,211
What are you looking at?

281
00:31:22,713 --> 00:31:24,465
Goodness, is that the time?

282
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:28,344
Sorry, Harry, I've got to leave you.
Dumbledore will want his...

283
00:31:29,011 --> 00:31:30,763
...well, he'll want to see me.

284
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:33,683
Your train leaves in ten minutes.

285
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:37,854
Here's your ticket. Do what it says.
It's very important.

286
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:42,108
ONE WAY TICKET
PLATFORM 9 3/4

287
00:31:42,316 --> 00:31:44,527
Platform nine
and three-quarters?

288
00:31:44,735 --> 00:31:47,405
But, Hagrid, there must
be a mistake.

289
00:31:47,613 --> 00:31:51,951
It says platform 9 3/4.
That doesn't exist, does it?

290
00:32:05,715 --> 00:32:07,842
Stand clear of the doors!

291
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:13,097
Excuse me.

292
00:32:14,682 --> 00:32:17,185
Excuse me. Excuse me.

293
00:32:17,602 --> 00:32:20,480
- Down the passage on your left.
- Excuse me, sir.

294
00:32:20,688 --> 00:32:23,232
How do I get
to platform 9 3/4?

295
00:32:23,399 --> 00:32:27,153
- Nine and three-quarters? Think you're funny?
- Same every year.

296
00:32:27,361 --> 00:32:29,572
Packed with Muggles. Come on.

297
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:32,074
- Muggles?
- Platform 9 3/4, this way.

298
00:32:39,081 --> 00:32:41,584
All right, Percy, you first.

299
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:55,056
- Fred, you're next.
- He's not Fred, I am.

300
00:32:55,264 --> 00:32:59,435
- Really! And you call yourself our mother.
- Oh, sorry, George.

301
00:33:03,606 --> 00:33:06,108
Just joking. I'm Fred.

302
00:33:11,822 --> 00:33:13,824
Excuse me.

303
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:17,328
Could you tell me...

304
00:33:17,537 --> 00:33:20,873
- ...how to...
- Get onto the platform? Of course.

305
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:24,794
Don't worry, dear.
It's Ron's first time too.

306
00:33:25,002 --> 00:33:28,965
All you have to do is walk straight
at the wall...

307
00:33:29,131 --> 00:33:30,841
...between platforms nine and ten.

308
00:33:31,050 --> 00:33:34,470
- Best run if you're nervous.
- Good luck.

309
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:06,544
HOGWARTS EXPRESS

310
00:34:32,069 --> 00:34:33,362
Excuse me.

311
00:34:33,696 --> 00:34:36,407
Mind if I sit here?
The train's full.

312
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:38,743
Not at all.

313
00:34:41,954 --> 00:34:44,373
I'm Ron.
Ron Weasley.

314
00:34:44,540 --> 00:34:46,042
I'm Harry. Harry Potter.

315
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:50,671
So... it's true?

316
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:54,175
I mean, do you really have the...?

317
00:34:54,383 --> 00:34:56,177
The what?

318
00:34:56,469 --> 00:34:59,597
- The scar?
- Oh, yes.

319
00:35:00,056 --> 00:35:02,016
Brilliant!

320
00:35:04,894 --> 00:35:07,897
- Anything from the trolley?
- No, thanks.

321
00:35:08,230 --> 00:35:10,066
I've got everything I need.

322
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:15,905
We'll take the lot.

323
00:35:27,124 --> 00:35:29,085
"Bertie Bott's
Every Flavor Beans"?

324
00:35:29,251 --> 00:35:31,420
They really do come
in every flavor.

325
00:35:32,296 --> 00:35:35,883
There's chocolate and peppermint.
There's also...

326
00:35:36,092 --> 00:35:39,053
...spinach, liver and tripe.

327
00:35:39,970 --> 00:35:43,349
George swears he once got
a bogey-flavored one.

328
00:35:48,771 --> 00:35:51,774
- Are these frogs real?
- It's just a spell.

329
00:35:51,941 --> 00:35:54,276
Besides, the cards
are what matter.

330
00:35:54,443 --> 00:35:58,239
Each pack has a famous witch
or wizard. I've got about 500.

331
00:36:01,367 --> 00:36:03,077
Watch out!

332
00:36:05,746 --> 00:36:09,458
Oh, bad luck.
They've only got one good jump in them.

333
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:15,923
- I've got Dumbledore!
- I've got about six of him.

334
00:36:17,925 --> 00:36:19,552
Hey, he's disappeared!

335
00:36:19,760 --> 00:36:23,180
You can't expect him
to hang around all day.

336
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,349
Meet Scabbers.

337
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:28,310
- Pathetic, isn't he?
- Just a little.

338
00:36:28,519 --> 00:36:31,897
Fred gave me a spell to turn him
yellow. Want to see?

339
00:36:32,148 --> 00:36:33,816
Yeah.

340
00:36:38,237 --> 00:36:39,905
Sunshine...

341
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:44,785
Has anyone seen a toad?
A boy named Neville's lost his.

342
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:46,787
No.

343
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:49,373
Are you doing magic?
Let's see it, then.

344
00:36:51,584 --> 00:36:55,838
<i>Sunshine, daisies,
butter mellow</i>

345
00:36:56,046 --> 00:36:58,799
<i>Turn this stupid,
fat rat yellow</i>

346
00:37:01,969 --> 00:37:04,472
Are you sure that's
a real spell?

347
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:06,891
It isn't very good, is it?

348
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:11,020
Of course, I've only tried
a few simple ones...

349
00:37:11,228 --> 00:37:13,189
...but they've all worked for me.

350
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:19,195
For example:

351
00:37:19,653 --> 00:37:21,864
<i>Oculus Reparo!</i>

352
00:37:24,867 --> 00:37:26,952
That's better, isn't it?

353
00:37:28,662 --> 00:37:32,208
Goodness, you're Harry Potter!

354
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:34,335
I'm Hermione Granger.

355
00:37:34,543 --> 00:37:36,378
And you are...?

356
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:40,424
- I'm Ron Weasley.
- Pleasure.

357
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:44,553
You'd better put your robes on.
We'll be arriving soon.

358
00:37:49,642 --> 00:37:53,229
You've got dirt on your nose.
Did you know?

359
00:37:53,395 --> 00:37:55,356
Right there.

360
00:38:07,576 --> 00:38:09,411
All right. First years.

361
00:38:09,745 --> 00:38:11,580
This way, please.

362
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:13,582
First-year students,
don't be shy.

363
00:38:14,416 --> 00:38:16,877
Come on, hurry up. Move along!

364
00:38:23,843 --> 00:38:26,762
- Hi, Harry.
- Hi, Hagrid.

365
00:38:27,930 --> 00:38:31,433
This way to the boats. Follow me.

366
00:39:17,897 --> 00:39:19,732
Excellent.

367
00:39:47,968 --> 00:39:50,262
Welcome to Hogwarts.

368
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:54,266
In a moment, you'll pass through
these doors and join your classmates.

369
00:39:54,475 --> 00:39:59,688
But before you take your seats,
you must be sorted into your houses.

370
00:39:59,897 --> 00:40:03,025
They are Gryffindor, Hufflepuff...

371
00:40:03,233 --> 00:40:06,362
...Ravenclaw and Slytherin.

372
00:40:08,155 --> 00:40:10,366
While you're here...

373
00:40:10,574 --> 00:40:13,118
...your house will be like your family.

374
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:16,747
Your triumphs will earn
your house points.

375
00:40:17,164 --> 00:40:20,834
Breaking the rules
will cost your house points.

376
00:40:21,794 --> 00:40:25,547
At the end of the year,
the house with the most points...

377
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:28,550
- ...wins the House Cup.
- Trevor!

378
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:39,311
Sorry.

379
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:42,731
The Sorting Ceremony
will begin in a moment.

380
00:40:44,566 --> 00:40:48,070
So it's true what they've been
saying on the train.

381
00:40:48,404 --> 00:40:52,658
- Harry Potter has come to Hogwarts.
- Harry Potter!

382
00:40:53,409 --> 00:40:57,579
These are Crabbe and Goyle.
I'm Malfoy.

383
00:40:58,747 --> 00:41:01,083
Draco Malfoy.

384
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:06,755
Think my name's funny?
I don't need to ask yours.

385
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:12,177
Red hair and a hand-me-down robe.
You must be a Weasley.

386
00:41:13,595 --> 00:41:17,516
You'll soon find some families
are better than others.

387
00:41:17,766 --> 00:41:21,103
You don't want to make friends
with the wrong sort.

388
00:41:21,770 --> 00:41:24,023
I can help you there.

389
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:28,986
I know how to tell
the right sort of people.

390
00:41:35,784 --> 00:41:37,953
We're ready for you.
Follow me.

391
00:41:56,555 --> 00:41:58,140
The ceiling isn't real.

392
00:41:58,307 --> 00:42:01,018
It's enchanted to look
like the night sky.

393
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:04,313
I read about it in
<i>Hogwarts: A History.</i>

394
00:42:17,618 --> 00:42:19,870
Would you wait here, please?

395
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:24,541
Now, before we begin...

396
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:28,003
...Professor Dumbledore would like
to say a few words.

397
00:42:28,253 --> 00:42:32,216
I have a few start-of-term
notices to announce.

398
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:35,844
First years, please note...

399
00:42:36,011 --> 00:42:41,100
...that the Dark Forest is
strictly forbidden to all students.

400
00:42:42,101 --> 00:42:45,604
Also, our caretaker,
Mr. Filch...

401
00:42:45,813 --> 00:42:47,815
...has asked me to remind you...

402
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:52,402
...that the third-floor corridor
on the right-hand side is out of bounds...

403
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:56,698
...unless you wish to suffer
a most painful death.

404
00:42:58,325 --> 00:42:59,868
Thank you.

405
00:43:02,037 --> 00:43:04,373
When I call your name...

406
00:43:04,581 --> 00:43:06,333
...you will come forward...

407
00:43:06,542 --> 00:43:09,586
...I shall place the Sorting Hat
on your head...

408
00:43:10,129 --> 00:43:12,714
...and you'll be sorted into your houses.

409
00:43:13,549 --> 00:43:15,717
Hermione Granger.

410
00:43:18,512 --> 00:43:21,056
Oh, no. All right, relax.

411
00:43:21,473 --> 00:43:24,101
She's completely mad, that one.
I'm telling you.

412
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:34,111
Ah, yes. All right.

413
00:43:34,444 --> 00:43:37,739
Well then. Gryffindor!

414
00:43:46,707 --> 00:43:48,417
Draco Malfoy.

415
00:43:54,089 --> 00:43:56,091
Slytherin!

416
00:43:57,217 --> 00:44:00,262
Every witch or wizard who went bad
came from there.

417
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:02,598
Susan Bones.

418
00:44:11,523 --> 00:44:15,194
- Harry, what's wrong?
- Nothing.

419
00:44:15,736 --> 00:44:18,280
- Nothing, I'm fine.
- Let's see.

420
00:44:18,488 --> 00:44:19,990
I know.

421
00:44:20,199 --> 00:44:21,992
Hufflepuff!

422
00:44:24,286 --> 00:44:26,538
Ronald Weasley.

423
00:44:40,802 --> 00:44:45,891
Another Weasley.
I know exactly what to do with you.

424
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,644
Gryffindor!

425
00:44:55,025 --> 00:44:57,152
Harry Potter.

426
00:45:15,587 --> 00:45:18,674
Difficult. Very difficult.

427
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:22,844
Plenty of courage, I see.
Not a bad mind either.

428
00:45:23,053 --> 00:45:25,514
There's talent, oh yes.

429
00:45:25,681 --> 00:45:29,268
And a thirst to prove yourself.

430
00:45:29,559 --> 00:45:32,354
But where to put you?

431
00:45:32,562 --> 00:45:35,023
Not Slytherin.
Not Slytherin.

432
00:45:35,190 --> 00:45:37,192
Not Slytherin, eh?

433
00:45:37,484 --> 00:45:40,737
Are you sure? You could be
great, you know.

434
00:45:40,946 --> 00:45:43,949
It's all here, in your head.

435
00:45:44,157 --> 00:45:49,621
And Slytherin will help you
on the way to greatness, no doubt.

436
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:54,418
No? Well, if you're sure.

437
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:56,461
Better be...

438
00:45:56,670 --> 00:45:58,463
...Gryffindor!

439
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:26,450
Your attention, please.

440
00:46:28,827 --> 00:46:31,496
Let the feast begin.

441
00:46:48,430 --> 00:46:50,140
I'm half-and-half.

442
00:46:50,349 --> 00:46:53,518
My dad's a Muggle,
my mum's a witch.

443
00:46:53,727 --> 00:46:56,480
He got quite a shock
when he found out.

444
00:46:58,148 --> 00:47:01,943
Percy, who's the professor
talking to Quirrell?

445
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,447
Professor Snape,
head of Slytherin House.

446
00:47:05,655 --> 00:47:07,616
- What does he teach?
- Potions.

447
00:47:07,824 --> 00:47:09,951
But he wants to teach
the Dark Arts.

448
00:47:10,118 --> 00:47:12,621
He's been after Quirrell's job
for years.

449
00:47:17,876 --> 00:47:22,506
Hello! How are you?
Welcome to Gryffindor.

450
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:35,852
Look!
It's the Bloody Baron!

451
00:47:41,066 --> 00:47:43,151
Hello, Sir Nicholas.
Have a nice summer?

452
00:47:44,027 --> 00:47:48,824
Dreadful. They wouldn't let me join
the Headless Hunt again.

453
00:47:52,452 --> 00:47:55,497
I know you.
You're Nearly Headless Nick.

454
00:47:55,664 --> 00:47:58,375
I prefer Sir Nicholas,
if you don't mind.

455
00:47:58,583 --> 00:48:02,087
Nearly headless?
How can you be nearly headless?

456
00:48:02,337 --> 00:48:03,797
Like this.

457
00:48:14,391 --> 00:48:17,811
Gryffindors, follow me, please.
Don't fall behind. Thank you.

458
00:48:18,437 --> 00:48:20,355
Ravenclaw, follow me.

459
00:48:21,022 --> 00:48:22,774
This way.

460
00:48:23,024 --> 00:48:26,194
This is the most direct route
to the dormitories.

461
00:48:26,361 --> 00:48:29,865
But watch out for the stairs.
They like to change.

462
00:48:39,875 --> 00:48:42,294
Don't lag behind, please.
Follow me.

463
00:48:42,669 --> 00:48:45,380
Quickly! Come on!

464
00:48:45,547 --> 00:48:48,008
Seamus, that picture moved.

465
00:48:48,800 --> 00:48:51,636
- Look at that one, Harry.
- I think she likes you.

466
00:48:54,055 --> 00:48:56,475
- Look! Look!
- Who's that girl?

467
00:48:56,683 --> 00:48:59,060
Welcome to Hogwarts.

468
00:49:15,035 --> 00:49:16,745
Password?

469
00:49:17,120 --> 00:49:19,289
Caput Draconis.

470
00:49:21,917 --> 00:49:22,918
Wow!

471
00:49:26,671 --> 00:49:30,717
Follow me, don't fall behind.
Quickly, come on!

472
00:49:34,304 --> 00:49:36,139
Gather round here.

473
00:49:38,475 --> 00:49:41,061
Welcome to the Gryffindor
common room.

474
00:49:41,937 --> 00:49:44,439
Boys' dormitories,
upstairs and to your left.

475
00:49:44,648 --> 00:49:46,525
Girls', the same, to your right.

476
00:49:46,733 --> 00:49:49,402
Your belongings are already
in your rooms.

477
00:50:57,012 --> 00:50:59,389
We're here!

478
00:50:59,806 --> 00:51:02,767
Can you imagine the old bat's face
if we'd been late?

479
00:51:07,439 --> 00:51:12,152
- That was brilliant!
- Thank you for that assessment.

480
00:51:12,652 --> 00:51:16,865
Perhaps it would be more useful
to turn you both into pocket watches?

481
00:51:17,198 --> 00:51:20,327
- Then one of you might be on time.
- We got lost.

482
00:51:20,535 --> 00:51:22,871
Then perhaps a map?

483
00:51:23,038 --> 00:51:26,041
Do you need one
to find your seats?

484
00:51:34,466 --> 00:51:39,387
You will not wave your wands foolishly
or cast silly spells in this class.

485
00:51:40,388 --> 00:51:45,060
I don't expect many of you
to appreciate the subtle science...

486
00:51:45,226 --> 00:51:47,395
...or the exact art
of potion-making.

487
00:51:47,604 --> 00:51:51,232
However, for the
select few...

488
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:55,487
...who possess the disposition...

489
00:51:59,032 --> 00:52:02,535
...I can teach you how
to bewitch the mind...

490
00:52:02,744 --> 00:52:05,538
...and ensnare the senses.

491
00:52:05,747 --> 00:52:09,584
I can tell you how to bottle fame,
brew glory...

492
00:52:09,793 --> 00:52:13,922
...and even stop death.

493
00:52:18,718 --> 00:52:23,181
On the other hand, perhaps some of you
have come to Hogwarts...

494
00:52:23,390 --> 00:52:25,850
...possessing such
formidable abilities...

495
00:52:26,059 --> 00:52:28,478
...and such confidence
in yourselves...

496
00:52:28,687 --> 00:52:32,273
...that you feel no need
to pay attention.

497
00:52:38,697 --> 00:52:40,323
Mr. Potter.

498
00:52:42,492 --> 00:52:46,287
Our new celebrity.

499
00:52:48,498 --> 00:52:52,961
What would I get if I added powdered
root of asphodel to an infusion of wormwood?

500
00:52:57,507 --> 00:53:00,135
Don't know? Well,
let's try again.

501
00:53:00,301 --> 00:53:03,304
Where would you look
if I asked you for a bezoar?

502
00:53:06,099 --> 00:53:07,475
I don't know, sir.

503
00:53:07,726 --> 00:53:10,395
And what's the difference
between monkshood and wolfsbane?

504
00:53:14,023 --> 00:53:16,317
I don't know, sir.

505
00:53:17,610 --> 00:53:19,446
Pity.

506
00:53:20,363 --> 00:53:24,659
Clearly, fame isn't everything...

507
00:53:25,368 --> 00:53:26,369
...is it, Mr. Potter?

508
00:53:30,415 --> 00:53:32,667
<i>Eye of rabbit,
harp string hum</i>

509
00:53:32,876 --> 00:53:35,670
<i>Turn this water
into rum</i>

510
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:39,424
<i>Eye of rabbit,
harp string hum</i>

511
00:53:39,632 --> 00:53:41,801
What's Seamus trying to do
with that glass of water?

512
00:53:42,010 --> 00:53:46,514
Turn it into rum. Yesterday he got
a kind of weak tea before he...

513
00:53:52,187 --> 00:53:54,856
Oh, the post is here.

514
00:54:27,722 --> 00:54:30,600
Can I borrow this?
Thanks.

515
00:54:34,145 --> 00:54:36,773
Look, Neville's got a Remembrall.

516
00:54:37,023 --> 00:54:40,193
I've read about those.
When the smoke turns red...

517
00:54:40,401 --> 00:54:42,403
...it means you've forgotten something.

518
00:54:42,862 --> 00:54:46,157
The trouble is, I never remember
what I've forgotten.

519
00:54:46,449 --> 00:54:51,329
Hey, Ron, someone's broken into Gringotts.
Listen to this:

520
00:54:51,538 --> 00:54:54,749
"Believed to be the work of
unknown Dark witches or wizards...

521
00:54:54,916 --> 00:54:57,418
...Gringotts goblins
confirmed the break-in...

522
00:54:57,585 --> 00:55:01,714
...stating that nothing was taken.
The vault in question, number 713...

523
00:55:01,923 --> 00:55:05,510
...had actually been emptied
earlier that same day."

524
00:55:05,969 --> 00:55:08,805
That's odd.
Hagrid and I went to that vault.

525
00:55:18,982 --> 00:55:22,944
- Good afternoon, class!
- Good afternoon, Madam Hooch.

526
00:55:23,111 --> 00:55:25,446
Good afternoon, Amanda.
Good afternoon.

527
00:55:27,073 --> 00:55:29,617
Welcome to your
first flying lesson.

528
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:33,872
Now, what are you waiting for?
Everyone stand to the left of your broom.

529
00:55:34,080 --> 00:55:35,832
Come on, hurry up!

530
00:55:36,332 --> 00:55:39,627
Right hand over your broom
and say, "Up."

531
00:55:39,836 --> 00:55:42,839
Up!

532
00:55:43,089 --> 00:55:44,173
Wow!

533
00:55:44,382 --> 00:55:45,800
Up!

534
00:55:47,927 --> 00:55:50,555
- Up! Up!
- Put some feeling into it.

535
00:55:50,763 --> 00:55:52,974
Up! Up!

536
00:55:53,308 --> 00:55:54,851
Up!

537
00:55:55,810 --> 00:55:57,312
Up!

538
00:55:57,478 --> 00:55:59,022
Up!

539
00:56:00,481 --> 00:56:02,275
Shut up, Harry.

540
00:56:02,692 --> 00:56:05,612
Now, once you've
got hold of your broom...

541
00:56:05,820 --> 00:56:08,865
...mount it and grip it tightly.

542
00:56:09,616 --> 00:56:11,576
You don't want to slide off the end.

543
00:56:11,951 --> 00:56:14,495
When I blow my whistle,
I want each of you...

544
00:56:14,662 --> 00:56:16,831
...to push off from the ground, hard.

545
00:56:17,081 --> 00:56:19,334
Keep your brooms steady...

546
00:56:19,500 --> 00:56:21,169
...hover for a moment...

547
00:56:21,336 --> 00:56:24,839
...lean forward slightly
and touch back down.

548
00:56:25,590 --> 00:56:28,343
On my whistle: Three, two...

549
00:56:31,304 --> 00:56:32,680
Mr. Longbottom.

550
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:40,188
- Mr... Mr... Mr. Longbottom!
- Come down, come down!

551
00:56:40,355 --> 00:56:44,025
- Watch out, Neville!
- Mr. Longbottom!

552
00:56:44,233 --> 00:56:46,778
- Help!
- Come down this instant!

553
00:56:55,036 --> 00:56:56,704
Help!

554
00:56:57,872 --> 00:56:59,040
Mr. Longb...

555
00:57:08,967 --> 00:57:10,218
Help!

556
00:57:17,058 --> 00:57:19,060
Everybody out of the way!

557
00:57:24,482 --> 00:57:25,775
- Come on.
- Is he all right?

558
00:57:27,402 --> 00:57:29,404
Oh, dear.
His wrist is broken.

559
00:57:30,446 --> 00:57:33,157
Poor boy, come on. Get up.

560
00:57:34,409 --> 00:57:39,247
Everyone keep your feet on the ground
while I take him to the hospital wing.

561
00:57:39,455 --> 00:57:40,623
Understood?

562
00:57:40,832 --> 00:57:43,084
If I see a single broom
in the air...

563
00:57:43,292 --> 00:57:47,463
...the offender will be expelled
before they can say "Quidditch."

564
00:57:48,715 --> 00:57:50,633
Did you see his face?

565
00:57:50,842 --> 00:57:53,011
Maybe if the fat lump
had squeezed this...

566
00:57:53,219 --> 00:57:56,389
- ...he'd remember how to land on his backside.
- Give that here, Malfoy.

567
00:57:58,182 --> 00:58:01,936
No, I'll leave it somewhere
for Longbottom to find.

568
00:58:06,024 --> 00:58:08,026
How about on the roof?

569
00:58:09,819 --> 00:58:13,031
What's the matter, Potter?
A little out of your reach?

570
00:58:15,950 --> 00:58:19,120
Harry, don't. You heard what Madam Hooch said.

571
00:58:19,328 --> 00:58:21,831
Besides, you don't even know how to fly.

572
00:58:23,166 --> 00:58:25,209
What an idiot.

573
00:58:28,588 --> 00:58:31,382
Give it back, Malfoy,
or I'll knock you off your broom!

574
00:58:32,175 --> 00:58:34,135
Really?

575
00:58:37,430 --> 00:58:39,390
Have it your way.

576
00:59:13,508 --> 00:59:15,927
That was amazing.

577
00:59:16,427 --> 00:59:18,513
Harry Potter!

578
00:59:19,388 --> 00:59:21,224
Follow me.

579
00:59:33,152 --> 00:59:35,196
Wait here.

580
00:59:37,156 --> 00:59:38,991
Professor Quirrell, excuse me.

581
00:59:39,200 --> 00:59:41,536
Could I borrow Wood for a moment,
please?

582
00:59:42,578 --> 00:59:44,455
Yes, of course.

583
00:59:49,877 --> 00:59:51,921
Potter, meet Oliver Wood.

584
00:59:52,380 --> 00:59:55,883
Wood, I've found you
a Seeker.

585
00:59:58,052 --> 01:00:01,556
Have you heard? Harry Potter's
the new Gryffindor Seeker.

586
01:00:01,764 --> 01:00:03,891
I knew he'd do well.

587
01:00:04,433 --> 01:00:08,563
Seeker? But first years
never make the house teams.

588
01:00:08,771 --> 01:00:11,065
You must be the youngest
Quidditch player...

589
01:00:11,274 --> 01:00:13,484
In a century, according to McGonagall.

590
01:00:13,693 --> 01:00:15,903
Congratulations, Harry.
Wood told us.

591
01:00:16,195 --> 01:00:18,865
Fred and George are
the team Beaters.

592
01:00:19,073 --> 01:00:22,743
Our job is to keep you
from getting hurt too badly.

593
01:00:22,910 --> 01:00:25,621
No promises, though.
It's a rough game.

594
01:00:25,830 --> 01:00:29,709
Brutal, but no one's died in years.
Someone disappears occasionally.

595
01:00:29,917 --> 01:00:32,420
But they turn up, in a month or two.

596
01:00:33,171 --> 01:00:37,425
Cheer up, Harry. Quidditch is
brilliant, the best game there is.

597
01:00:37,592 --> 01:00:40,678
- And you'll be amazing.
- But I've never played.

598
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:44,640
- What if I make a fool of myself?
- You won't make a fool of yourself.

599
01:00:44,849 --> 01:00:46,767
It's in your blood.

600
01:00:54,108 --> 01:00:55,484
SEEKER
JAMES POTTER

601
01:00:55,693 --> 01:00:59,071
You never told me your dad
was a Seeker.

602
01:00:59,280 --> 01:01:01,782
I didn't know.

603
01:01:07,163 --> 01:01:11,751
I'm telling you, it's creepy.
She knows more about you than you do!

604
01:01:11,959 --> 01:01:13,544
Who doesn't?

605
01:01:15,213 --> 01:01:16,964
What's happening?

606
01:01:17,506 --> 01:01:20,676
The staircases change.
Remember?

607
01:01:27,141 --> 01:01:30,561
- Let's go this way.
- Before the staircase moves.

608
01:01:39,237 --> 01:01:42,698
Does anyone else feel like
we shouldn't be here?

609
01:01:42,907 --> 01:01:47,662
That's because we shouldn't be.
It's the third floor. It's forbidden.

610
01:01:50,289 --> 01:01:51,832
Let's go.

611
01:01:54,043 --> 01:01:56,087
- It's Filch's cat!
- Run!

612
01:02:00,675 --> 01:02:03,636
Quick, let's hide
through that door!

613
01:02:09,141 --> 01:02:11,519
- It's locked!
- We're done for!

614
01:02:11,727 --> 01:02:13,688
Oh, move over!

615
01:02:14,605 --> 01:02:16,565
<i>Alohomora!</i>

616
01:02:17,525 --> 01:02:18,693
Get in!

617
01:02:20,778 --> 01:02:24,573
<i>- Alohomora?
- Standard Book of Spells, Chapter Seven.</i>

618
01:02:24,782 --> 01:02:27,535
Is anybody here, my sweet?

619
01:02:34,458 --> 01:02:35,459
Come on.

620
01:02:36,335 --> 01:02:38,629
- Filch is gone.
- He thought it was locked.

621
01:02:38,838 --> 01:02:41,882
- It was locked.
- And for good reason.

622
01:03:01,861 --> 01:03:03,738
Push! Come on!

623
01:03:08,242 --> 01:03:10,036
How can they possibly...

624
01:03:10,244 --> 01:03:13,914
...keep a thing like that
locked up in a school?

625
01:03:14,123 --> 01:03:17,793
Don't you use your eyes?
Didn't you see what it was standing on?

626
01:03:18,002 --> 01:03:22,089
I wasn't looking at its feet. I was
a little preoccupied with its heads.

627
01:03:22,298 --> 01:03:25,259
Or perhaps you didn't notice:
It had three!

628
01:03:25,468 --> 01:03:29,138
It was standing on a trapdoor.
It wasn't there by accident.

629
01:03:29,347 --> 01:03:31,182
It's guarding something.

630
01:03:31,640 --> 01:03:34,101
- Guarding something?
- Exactly.

631
01:03:34,310 --> 01:03:37,021
Now, if you don't mind,
I'm going to bed...

632
01:03:37,229 --> 01:03:40,608
...before you come up with
another brilliant idea to get us killed.

633
01:03:40,775 --> 01:03:43,444
Or worse,
expelled.

634
01:03:47,323 --> 01:03:50,743
She needs to sort out her priorities.

635
01:03:56,248 --> 01:04:00,461
Quidditch is easy to understand.
Seven players on each side.

636
01:04:00,711 --> 01:04:02,505
Three Chasers, two Beaters...

637
01:04:02,922 --> 01:04:05,925
...one Keeper and one Seeker.
That's you.

638
01:04:11,639 --> 01:04:13,557
There are three kinds of balls.

639
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:15,726
This ball is the Quaffle.

640
01:04:15,935 --> 01:04:18,437
The Chasers throw the Quaffle...

641
01:04:18,646 --> 01:04:21,190
...and try to get it
through those three hoops.

642
01:04:21,982 --> 01:04:26,570
The Keeper, that's me, defends
the hoops. Following me so far?

643
01:04:26,779 --> 01:04:28,406
I think so.

644
01:04:28,739 --> 01:04:30,574
What are those called?

645
01:04:33,369 --> 01:04:35,246
Take this.

646
01:04:45,673 --> 01:04:47,216
Watch out, it'll come back.

647
01:04:55,015 --> 01:04:57,017
Not bad, Potter.

648
01:04:57,476 --> 01:04:59,520
You'd make a good Beater.

649
01:05:15,202 --> 01:05:17,163
What was that?

650
01:05:18,205 --> 01:05:21,542
Those are Bludgers. They're nasty.

651
01:05:22,042 --> 01:05:24,753
But you're a Seeker.

652
01:05:29,258 --> 01:05:33,262
The only thing I want
you worrying about is this.

653
01:05:34,054 --> 01:05:36,182
The Golden Snitch.

654
01:05:37,099 --> 01:05:39,935
- I like this ball.
- You like it now.

655
01:05:40,144 --> 01:05:44,315
You'll see. It's very fast
and almost impossible to spot.

656
01:05:44,523 --> 01:05:46,233
What do I do with it?

657
01:05:46,442 --> 01:05:49,778
Catch it before
the other team's Seeker.

658
01:05:49,987 --> 01:05:51,780
Catch it,
and the game's over.

659
01:05:52,656 --> 01:05:54,408
Catch it, Potter...

660
01:05:54,617 --> 01:05:56,243
...and we win.

661
01:06:05,711 --> 01:06:10,424
A basic skill
for wizards is levitation.

662
01:06:10,633 --> 01:06:14,637
Or the ability
to make objects fly.

663
01:06:14,845 --> 01:06:17,890
Have you got your feathers?
Good.

664
01:06:18,098 --> 01:06:22,811
Don't forget the wrist movement
we've been practicing.

665
01:06:23,020 --> 01:06:26,690
Swish and flick. Everyone.

666
01:06:27,358 --> 01:06:30,277
Swish and flick.

667
01:06:30,569 --> 01:06:32,863
Very good.
And pronounce it clearly.

668
01:06:33,572 --> 01:06:35,950
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

669
01:06:36,325 --> 01:06:37,826
Off you go.

670
01:06:39,286 --> 01:06:41,455
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

671
01:06:41,747 --> 01:06:43,958
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

672
01:06:44,166 --> 01:06:46,794
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

673
01:06:47,836 --> 01:06:52,258
Stop, stop, stop.
You'll take someone's eye out.

674
01:06:52,466 --> 01:06:56,637
Besides, you're saying it wrong.
It's Levi-o-sa.

675
01:06:56,845 --> 01:07:00,808
- Not Levio-sa.
- You do it, then, if you're so clever.

676
01:07:01,016 --> 01:07:02,768
Come on, come on.

677
01:07:04,395 --> 01:07:06,814
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

678
01:07:15,531 --> 01:07:17,116
Well done!

679
01:07:17,324 --> 01:07:20,578
Look, everyone.
Miss Granger's done it.

680
01:07:20,786 --> 01:07:22,079
Splendid!

681
01:07:22,288 --> 01:07:25,583
<i>- Wingardium Leviosa.
- Congratulations, my dear.</i>

682
01:07:30,504 --> 01:07:33,841
I think we're going to need
another feather here, Professor.

683
01:07:41,015 --> 01:07:45,352
<i>"It's Levi-o-sa. Not Levio-sa."</i>

684
01:07:45,519 --> 01:07:49,857
She's a nightmare.
No wonder she hasn't got any friends.

685
01:07:51,650 --> 01:07:53,235
I think she heard you.

686
01:08:23,057 --> 01:08:25,017
Where's Hermione?

687
01:08:25,225 --> 01:08:28,270
Parvati Patil said she wouldn't
come out of the girls' bathroom.

688
01:08:28,479 --> 01:08:31,774
Said she's been in there all afternoon, crying.

689
01:08:36,987 --> 01:08:40,407
Troll in the dungeon!

690
01:08:40,741 --> 01:08:43,577
Troll in the dungeon!

691
01:08:46,955 --> 01:08:49,416
Thought you ought to know.

692
01:08:56,256 --> 01:08:59,009
Silence!

693
01:09:00,594 --> 01:09:03,931
There is no need to panic.

694
01:09:05,307 --> 01:09:06,975
Now...

695
01:09:07,184 --> 01:09:11,689
...prefects will lead their houses
back to the dormitories.

696
01:09:12,314 --> 01:09:15,984
Teachers will follow me
to the dungeons.

697
01:09:28,163 --> 01:09:31,458
Gryffindors, don't fall behind,
please, and stay alert.

698
01:09:31,667 --> 01:09:33,502
How could a troll get in?

699
01:09:33,711 --> 01:09:36,296
With help.
Trolls are very stupid.

700
01:09:36,505 --> 01:09:38,632
Maybe someone's playing a joke.

701
01:09:38,966 --> 01:09:42,010
- What?
- Hermione. She doesn't know!

702
01:09:55,065 --> 01:09:57,651
I think the troll's left
the dungeon.

703
01:10:02,239 --> 01:10:04,324
It's going into
the girls' bathroom!

704
01:10:35,397 --> 01:10:37,441
Hermione, move!

705
01:10:41,069 --> 01:10:42,529
Help!

706
01:10:43,322 --> 01:10:44,990
Help!

707
01:10:47,284 --> 01:10:49,369
Hey, you great idiot!

708
01:11:01,799 --> 01:11:03,467
Help!

709
01:11:24,696 --> 01:11:26,865
Do something!

710
01:11:28,492 --> 01:11:30,118
What?

711
01:11:30,327 --> 01:11:31,829
Anything!

712
01:11:33,080 --> 01:11:35,624
Hurry up!
Swish and flick.

713
01:11:35,874 --> 01:11:38,085
<i>Wingardium Leviosa.</i>

714
01:11:48,971 --> 01:11:49,972
Brilliant.

715
01:12:15,455 --> 01:12:18,292
Is it... dead?

716
01:12:18,500 --> 01:12:21,795
I don't think so. It's just unconscious.

717
01:12:28,802 --> 01:12:30,804
Troll bogeys.

718
01:12:33,390 --> 01:12:35,100
Good heavens!

719
01:12:35,309 --> 01:12:38,562
- Explain yourselves, both of you!
- Well, you see...

720
01:12:38,770 --> 01:12:40,981
It was my fault, Professor McGonagall.

721
01:12:41,857 --> 01:12:43,317
What?

722
01:12:44,026 --> 01:12:46,028
Miss Granger?

723
01:12:46,236 --> 01:12:47,946
I went looking for the troll.

724
01:12:48,155 --> 01:12:50,866
I'd read about them and thought
I could handle it.

725
01:12:51,408 --> 01:12:53,452
But I was wrong.

726
01:12:53,660 --> 01:12:56,204
If Harry and Ron hadn't
come to find me...

727
01:12:56,872 --> 01:12:59,374
...I'd probably be dead.

728
01:12:59,583 --> 01:13:04,129
In any event, it was
an extremely foolish thing to do.

729
01:13:04,338 --> 01:13:07,174
I expected more sensible behavior
from you...

730
01:13:07,341 --> 01:13:09,885
...and I am very disappointed,
Miss Granger.

731
01:13:10,093 --> 01:13:12,512
Gryffindor will lose five points...

732
01:13:13,263 --> 01:13:16,391
...for your serious lack of judgment.

733
01:13:17,434 --> 01:13:19,478
As for you gentlemen...

734
01:13:19,686 --> 01:13:22,230
...I hope you realize
how lucky you are.

735
01:13:23,190 --> 01:13:26,693
Not many first-year students can
take on a fully grown troll...

736
01:13:26,902 --> 01:13:29,029
...and live to tell the tale.

737
01:13:29,655 --> 01:13:31,657
Five points...

738
01:13:33,450 --> 01:13:35,869
...to each of you...

739
01:13:38,121 --> 01:13:40,791
...for sheer dumb luck.

740
01:13:46,922 --> 01:13:50,050
You'd better go.
It m-might wake up.

741
01:13:58,892 --> 01:14:00,727
Eat some toast. Come on.

742
01:14:01,311 --> 01:14:04,690
Ron's right, Harry.
You'll need your strength today.

743
01:14:04,898 --> 01:14:06,858
I'm not hungry.

744
01:14:07,651 --> 01:14:09,736
Good luck today, Potter.

745
01:14:10,904 --> 01:14:13,156
Well, since you've proved your
bravery against a troll...

746
01:14:13,365 --> 01:14:16,201
...a game of Quidditch
should be easy.

747
01:14:16,785 --> 01:14:19,246
Even against Slytherin.

748
01:14:27,713 --> 01:14:29,673
That explains the blood.

749
01:14:30,132 --> 01:14:31,466
Blood?

750
01:14:31,675 --> 01:14:35,929
Last night, I think Snape let
the troll in as a distraction...

751
01:14:36,096 --> 01:14:38,432
...so he could confront
the three-headed dog.

752
01:14:38,640 --> 01:14:41,560
But the dog bit him.
That's why he's limping.

753
01:14:41,768 --> 01:14:43,937
Why would anyone want
to go near that dog?

754
01:14:44,438 --> 01:14:47,899
When I went to Gringotts,
Hagrid took something out of a vault.

755
01:14:48,108 --> 01:14:50,277
He said it was
secret Hogwarts business.

756
01:14:51,445 --> 01:14:54,281
- And you think...
- That's what the dog's guarding.

757
01:14:54,489 --> 01:14:56,533
That's what Snape wants.

758
01:15:10,380 --> 01:15:12,215
The post's early today, isn't it?

759
01:15:12,424 --> 01:15:14,468
I never get anything.

760
01:15:14,968 --> 01:15:16,511
Let's open it.

761
01:15:26,730 --> 01:15:28,607
It's a broom.

762
01:15:28,815 --> 01:15:32,903
It's not just any broom, Harry.
It's a Nimbus 2000!

763
01:15:34,321 --> 01:15:36,239
But who...?

764
01:15:58,011 --> 01:15:59,513
Are you scared, Harry?

765
01:15:59,721 --> 01:16:01,890
- A little.
- Don't worry.

766
01:16:02,182 --> 01:16:04,434
I was too, before my first match.

767
01:16:04,643 --> 01:16:06,353
How did it go?

768
01:16:06,937 --> 01:16:10,524
I don't remember.
A Bludger hit me on the head.

769
01:16:11,233 --> 01:16:13,068
Woke up in the hospital wing
a week later.

770
01:16:36,299 --> 01:16:39,761
Hello and welcome to the first
Quidditch match of the season.

771
01:16:39,970 --> 01:16:43,098
Today's match:
Slytherin versus Gryffindor!

772
01:16:49,396 --> 01:16:51,273
Gryffindor!

773
01:17:15,005 --> 01:17:17,924
The players take their positions
as Madam Hooch enters...

774
01:17:18,091 --> 01:17:21,011
...the pitch to start the match!

775
01:17:21,553 --> 01:17:24,514
I want a nice, clean game...

776
01:17:25,432 --> 01:17:27,726
...from all of you.

777
01:17:33,190 --> 01:17:36,067
And out come the Bludgers,
followed by the Golden Snitch.

778
01:17:36,276 --> 01:17:39,029
Remember, the Snitch
is worth 150 points.

779
01:17:39,237 --> 01:17:42,032
The Seeker who catches the Snitch
ends the game.

780
01:17:49,122 --> 01:17:52,125
The Quaffle is released,
and the match begins!

781
01:18:11,686 --> 01:18:15,023
Angelina Johnson scores!
Ten points to Gryffindor!

782
01:18:21,863 --> 01:18:23,156
Well done!

783
01:18:27,452 --> 01:18:29,579
Slytherin takes
possession of the Quaffle.

784
01:18:29,788 --> 01:18:32,332
Bletchley passes it
to the captain, Marcus Flint.

785
01:19:05,031 --> 01:19:07,742
Another ten points
for Gryffindor!

786
01:19:21,881 --> 01:19:23,383
Give me that!

787
01:19:55,206 --> 01:19:57,208
Get over there.

788
01:20:47,175 --> 01:20:49,636
What's happening
to Harry's broom?

789
01:20:59,521 --> 01:21:01,731
Snape is putting a spell
on the broom!

790
01:21:01,940 --> 01:21:05,151
- A spell? What do we do?
- I'll take care of it.

791
01:21:18,706 --> 01:21:20,083
What a shame!

792
01:21:28,174 --> 01:21:29,551
Hurry, Hermione!

793
01:21:43,523 --> 01:21:45,859
<i>Lacarnum Inflamarae.</i>

794
01:21:54,409 --> 01:21:57,495
Fire!
He's on fire!

795
01:22:14,679 --> 01:22:17,557
- Come on! Come on!
- Fly, fly!

796
01:23:09,526 --> 01:23:10,944
Looks like he's going to be sick.

797
01:23:13,154 --> 01:23:14,572
He's got the Snitch!

798
01:23:14,781 --> 01:23:18,618
Harry Potter earns 150 points
for catching the Snitch!

799
01:23:18,910 --> 01:23:20,620
Gryffindor wins!

800
01:23:29,420 --> 01:23:30,797
Hooray!

801
01:23:55,822 --> 01:23:59,158
Well done, Gryffindor!

802
01:23:59,367 --> 01:24:02,161
Well done, Gryffindor!

803
01:24:04,247 --> 01:24:06,040
Rubbish.

804
01:24:06,249 --> 01:24:09,502
- Why would he put a spell on the broom?
- Who knows?

805
01:24:09,669 --> 01:24:12,755
Why did he try to get past
the three-headed dog?

806
01:24:12,964 --> 01:24:15,300
- Who told you about Fluffy?
- Fluffy?

807
01:24:15,508 --> 01:24:19,178
- That thing has a name?
- Of course it has a name. It's mine.

808
01:24:19,387 --> 01:24:22,348
Bought him from an Irish fellow
in a pub.

809
01:24:22,557 --> 01:24:24,684
Then I lent him to
Dumbledore to guard...

810
01:24:24,851 --> 01:24:26,811
I've said too much. No questions.

811
01:24:27,020 --> 01:24:29,897
Don't ask me anything else.
That's top secret.

812
01:24:30,106 --> 01:24:34,068
I don't know what Fluffy's guarding,
but Snape wants to steal it.

813
01:24:34,277 --> 01:24:38,031
Rubbish. Professor Snape
is a teacher at Hogwarts.

814
01:24:38,239 --> 01:24:41,909
Teacher or not, I know
a curse when I see one.

815
01:24:42,118 --> 01:24:44,912
I've read all about them.
You need eye contact...

816
01:24:45,121 --> 01:24:48,458
- ...and Snape wasn't blinking.
- Exactly.

817
01:24:50,084 --> 01:24:53,004
Listen carefully, all three of you.

818
01:24:53,212 --> 01:24:55,590
You're meddling in things
that don't concern you.

819
01:24:56,382 --> 01:24:57,884
That's dangerous.

820
01:24:58,051 --> 01:25:02,388
What that dog is guarding is
Dumbledore and Nicolas Flamel's business.

821
01:25:03,222 --> 01:25:04,724
Nicolas Flamel?

822
01:25:05,767 --> 01:25:09,228
I shouldn't have said that.
I shouldn't have said that.

823
01:25:09,437 --> 01:25:12,065
- I shouldn't have said that.
- Nicolas Flamel.

824
01:25:12,774 --> 01:25:14,942
Who's Nicolas Flamel?

825
01:25:15,151 --> 01:25:16,819
I don't know.

826
01:25:35,797 --> 01:25:41,594
<i>Merry Christmas, merry Christmas,
ring the Hogwarts bell</i>

827
01:25:41,803 --> 01:25:45,431
<i>Merry Christmas, merry Christmas</i>

828
01:26:01,447 --> 01:26:03,866
Knight to E5.

829
01:26:12,375 --> 01:26:14,627
Queen to E5.

830
01:26:20,216 --> 01:26:22,135
That's barbaric!

831
01:26:22,343 --> 01:26:24,345
That's wizard's chess.

832
01:26:24,804 --> 01:26:27,473
- I see you've packed.
- I see you haven't.

833
01:26:27,724 --> 01:26:30,810
Change of plans.
My parents decided to go to Romania...

834
01:26:31,102 --> 01:26:34,480
...with my brother Charlie.
He's studying dragons.

835
01:26:34,981 --> 01:26:37,024
Right. You can
help Harry, then.

836
01:26:37,233 --> 01:26:40,820
He'll be in the library looking
for information on Nicolas Flamel.

837
01:26:41,028 --> 01:26:43,448
We've looked a hundred times.

838
01:26:45,032 --> 01:26:47,452
Not in the Restricted Section.

839
01:26:48,035 --> 01:26:49,746
Merry Christmas.

840
01:26:52,373 --> 01:26:55,334
I think we've been
a bad influence on her.

841
01:26:57,837 --> 01:27:01,424
Harry, wake up!
Come on, Harry, wake up!

842
01:27:12,018 --> 01:27:14,896
- Merry Christmas, Harry.
- Merry Christmas, Ron.

843
01:27:15,563 --> 01:27:17,648
What are you wearing?

844
01:27:18,399 --> 01:27:22,111
My mum made it.
You've got one too.

845
01:27:23,237 --> 01:27:25,698
- I got presents?
- Yeah.

846
01:27:33,080 --> 01:27:34,791
There they are.

847
01:27:46,385 --> 01:27:49,597
"Your father left this
in my possession before he died.

848
01:27:49,806 --> 01:27:51,933
It is time I returned it to you.

849
01:27:52,350 --> 01:27:54,060
Use it well."

850
01:28:10,743 --> 01:28:14,580
- What is it?
- It's some kind of cloak.

851
01:28:14,872 --> 01:28:16,582
Let's see. Put it on.

852
01:28:23,339 --> 01:28:26,551
- My body's disappeared!
- I know what it is.

853
01:28:26,759 --> 01:28:30,471
- It's an invisibility cloak!
- Am I invisible?

854
01:28:31,222 --> 01:28:33,057
They're very rare.

855
01:28:34,600 --> 01:28:37,645
- Who could have given it to you?
- There was no signature.

856
01:28:37,854 --> 01:28:40,940
It only said, "Use it well."

857
01:28:52,368 --> 01:28:54,996
RESTRICTED SECTION

858
01:29:09,051 --> 01:29:14,223
<i>Famous Fire-Eaters.
Villains of the Fifteenth Century.</i>

859
01:29:14,974 --> 01:29:19,979
Flamel. Nicolas Flamel.
Where are you?

860
01:29:39,707 --> 01:29:41,417
Who's there?

861
01:29:47,715 --> 01:29:49,550
I know you're there.

862
01:29:50,509 --> 01:29:52,762
You can't hide.

863
01:30:00,770 --> 01:30:04,273
Who is it?
Show yourself!

864
01:30:51,737 --> 01:30:53,906
Severus, I-I...

865
01:30:54,073 --> 01:30:57,535
I wouldn't advise you
to make an enemy of me, Quirrell.

866
01:30:59,078 --> 01:31:01,163
- I don't know what you mean.
- You know perfectly well.

867
01:31:19,765 --> 01:31:22,643
We'll have another
little chat soon.

868
01:31:23,102 --> 01:31:28,065
When you've decided
where your loyalties lie.

869
01:31:28,899 --> 01:31:30,443
Professors.

870
01:31:30,651 --> 01:31:33,362
I found this
in the Restricted Section.

871
01:31:33,904 --> 01:31:37,950
It's still warm.
There's a student out of bed.

872
01:33:11,043 --> 01:33:13,170
Mum?

873
01:33:16,048 --> 01:33:18,217
Dad?

874
01:33:52,751 --> 01:33:56,630
Ron, you really have
to see this! You have to see it!

875
01:33:59,550 --> 01:34:03,429
- Ron, come on, get up!
- Why?

876
01:34:03,637 --> 01:34:06,265
There's something you need to see. Come on.

877
01:34:13,022 --> 01:34:14,356
Come on!

878
01:34:14,565 --> 01:34:16,567
Look, it's my parents.

879
01:34:18,777 --> 01:34:20,779
I only see the two of us.

880
01:34:20,988 --> 01:34:23,616
Look closely. Stand there.

881
01:34:24,533 --> 01:34:26,619
There. You see them, don't you?

882
01:34:26,827 --> 01:34:30,456
That's me! And I've won
the annual award.

883
01:34:30,956 --> 01:34:33,292
And I'm holding
the Quidditch Cup.

884
01:34:33,500 --> 01:34:37,713
And, blimey, I'm
Quidditch captain too.

885
01:34:38,797 --> 01:34:40,591
I look good.

886
01:34:41,967 --> 01:34:45,846
Harry, do you think this
mirror shows the future?

887
01:34:46,055 --> 01:34:49,934
How can it?
Both my parents are dead.

888
01:35:14,041 --> 01:35:16,210
Back again, Harry?

889
01:35:19,338 --> 01:35:21,840
I see that you,
like many before you...

890
01:35:22,049 --> 01:35:25,177
...have discovered the delights
of the Mirror of Erised.

891
01:35:26,512 --> 01:35:30,391
I hope you've realized
what it does.

892
01:35:32,017 --> 01:35:34,270
Let me give you a clue.

893
01:35:35,104 --> 01:35:37,273
The happiest man
on earth...

894
01:35:37,523 --> 01:35:43,529
...would look in the mirror and
see himself exactly as he is.

895
01:35:43,737 --> 01:35:46,949
So it shows us
what we want?

896
01:35:47,157 --> 01:35:51,537
- Whatever we desire?
- Yes, and no.

897
01:35:52,538 --> 01:35:55,124
It shows us nothing more
and nothing less...

898
01:35:55,332 --> 01:36:00,587
...than the deepest, most desperate
desires of our hearts.

899
01:36:01,422 --> 01:36:04,883
You, Harry, who have
never known your family...

900
01:36:06,385 --> 01:36:10,055
...see them standing beside you.

901
01:36:10,556 --> 01:36:12,558
But remember this, Harry...

902
01:36:13,142 --> 01:36:15,352
...this mirror...

903
01:36:15,561 --> 01:36:20,357
...gives us neither
knowledge nor truth.

904
01:36:22,276 --> 01:36:25,696
Men have wasted away
in front of it.

905
01:36:25,904 --> 01:36:28,324
Some have even gone mad.

906
01:36:29,366 --> 01:36:33,537
For that reason, tomorrow
it will be moved to a new location.

907
01:36:33,746 --> 01:36:35,664
And I must ask you...

908
01:36:36,415 --> 01:36:39,835
...not to look for it again.

909
01:36:41,253 --> 01:36:44,340
It does not do to dwell
on dreams...

910
01:36:44,923 --> 01:36:47,676
...and forget to live.

911
01:37:43,273 --> 01:37:44,733
I told you we were looking
in the wrong section.

912
01:37:44,942 --> 01:37:47,736
How could I have been so stupid?

913
01:37:48,362 --> 01:37:51,073
I checked this out weeks ago
for some light reading.

914
01:37:51,740 --> 01:37:53,742
This is light reading?

915
01:37:58,831 --> 01:38:00,999
Of course, here it is!

916
01:38:01,166 --> 01:38:05,003
"Nicolas Flamel is the only known
maker of the Sorcerer's Stone."

917
01:38:05,337 --> 01:38:07,047
The what?

918
01:38:07,256 --> 01:38:09,842
Honestly, don't you ever read?

919
01:38:10,259 --> 01:38:12,845
"The Sorcerer's Stone is
a legendary substance...

920
01:38:13,011 --> 01:38:14,972
...with astonishing powers.

921
01:38:15,180 --> 01:38:19,518
It transforms any metal into pure gold
and produces the Elixir of Life...

922
01:38:19,852 --> 01:38:23,021
- ...which makes the drinker immortal."
- Immortal?

923
01:38:23,188 --> 01:38:26,233
- It means you never die.
- I know what it means!

924
01:38:27,359 --> 01:38:29,862
"The only Stone currently
in existence...

925
01:38:30,028 --> 01:38:33,449
...belongs to Mr. Nicolas Flamel,
the noted alchemist...

926
01:38:33,657 --> 01:38:37,411
...who celebrated his
665th birthday last year."

927
01:38:39,037 --> 01:38:43,292
That's what Fluffy's guarding.
That's what's beneath the trapdoor.

928
01:38:43,500 --> 01:38:45,544
The Sorcerer's Stone.

929
01:39:03,896 --> 01:39:06,899
Sorry, I don't mean to be rude,
but I can't have visitors today.

930
01:39:07,065 --> 01:39:09,067
We know about
the Sorcerer's Stone!

931
01:39:14,573 --> 01:39:17,201
- We think Snape wants to steal it.
- Snape?

932
01:39:17,409 --> 01:39:19,620
Are you still obsessed with him?

933
01:39:19,828 --> 01:39:22,581
He wants the Stone, though
we don't know why.

934
01:39:22,998 --> 01:39:26,001
Snape is one of the teachers
protecting the Stone.

935
01:39:26,210 --> 01:39:28,295
- He's not going to steal it.
- What?

936
01:39:28,504 --> 01:39:30,714
You heard me. Please...

937
01:39:30,923 --> 01:39:33,634
- ...I'm rather busy today.
- Wait a moment.

938
01:39:33,842 --> 01:39:36,094
- One of the teachers?
- Of course!

939
01:39:36,303 --> 01:39:38,764
There are other things
protecting the Stone, aren't there?

940
01:39:38,931 --> 01:39:41,934
- Spells, enchantments.
- That's right.

941
01:39:42,142 --> 01:39:44,937
A big waste of time,
if you ask me.

942
01:39:45,145 --> 01:39:47,606
Nobody's getting past Fluffy.

943
01:39:47,773 --> 01:39:51,109
Nobody knows how,
except me and Dumbledore.

944
01:39:51,693 --> 01:39:53,946
I shouldn't have told you that.

945
01:40:08,961 --> 01:40:14,132
- Hagrid, what exactly is that?
- That? It's, uh... it's...

946
01:40:14,299 --> 01:40:16,468
I know what that is!

947
01:40:16,677 --> 01:40:19,221
But, Hagrid,
how did you get one?

948
01:40:19,429 --> 01:40:22,766
Won it. In a bet
with a stranger at the pub.

949
01:40:22,975 --> 01:40:25,978
To tell the truth, I think he was
glad to get rid of it.

950
01:40:49,167 --> 01:40:50,961
Is that a...?

951
01:40:52,462 --> 01:40:55,716
- ...dragon?
- It's not just any dragon.

952
01:40:55,924 --> 01:40:58,260
It's a Norwegian Ridgeback.

953
01:40:58,468 --> 01:41:01,305
My brother Charlie works
with them in Romania.

954
01:41:01,513 --> 01:41:02,889
Isn't he beautiful?

955
01:41:03,348 --> 01:41:05,601
Bless him. Look,
he knows his mummy.

956
01:41:06,935 --> 01:41:08,729
Hello, Norbert.

957
01:41:09,021 --> 01:41:12,357
- Norbert?
- He needs a name, doesn't he?

958
01:41:14,026 --> 01:41:16,320
Don't you, Norbert?

959
01:41:23,660 --> 01:41:26,204
I'll have to train him, of course.

960
01:41:30,500 --> 01:41:32,586
Who's that?

961
01:41:34,296 --> 01:41:36,089
Malfoy!

962
01:41:37,132 --> 01:41:38,592
Oh, dear.

963
01:41:40,218 --> 01:41:44,556
Hagrid always wanted a dragon.
He told me when we first met.

964
01:41:45,432 --> 01:41:47,059
It's mad.

965
01:41:47,225 --> 01:41:50,604
- And worse, Malfoy knows.
- I don't understand.

966
01:41:50,812 --> 01:41:53,273
- Is that bad?
- It's bad.

967
01:41:53,899 --> 01:41:55,901
Good evening.

968
01:41:59,738 --> 01:42:02,741
Nothing, I repeat, nothing...

969
01:42:02,908 --> 01:42:06,495
...gives a student the right
to wander the school at night.

970
01:42:06,703 --> 01:42:09,331
Therefore, as punishment
for your actions...

971
01:42:09,539 --> 01:42:11,541
...you will lose fifty points.

972
01:42:11,750 --> 01:42:14,086
- Fifty?
- Each.

973
01:42:15,128 --> 01:42:17,589
And to make sure
it doesn't happen again...

974
01:42:17,798 --> 01:42:20,634
...the four of you will serve detention
after classes.

975
01:42:21,843 --> 01:42:24,930
Excuse me, Professor,
perhaps I misheard you.

976
01:42:25,138 --> 01:42:27,557
I thought I heard "the four of you."

977
01:42:27,766 --> 01:42:30,227
No, you heard me correctly,
Mr. Malfoy.

978
01:42:30,435 --> 01:42:35,357
Despite your honorable intentions,
you were out of bed too.

979
01:42:35,857 --> 01:42:38,777
You'll serve the same detention
as your classmates.

980
01:42:49,955 --> 01:42:53,291
It's a pity they did away
with the old punishments.

981
01:42:53,792 --> 01:42:58,296
I remember when they used to hang them
by their thumbs after class.

982
01:42:59,047 --> 01:43:01,383
Goodness, how I miss the screaming.

983
01:43:04,469 --> 01:43:07,723
You'll be serving detention
with Hagrid tonight.

984
01:43:07,973 --> 01:43:12,394
He's got a little job to do
in the Dark Forest.

985
01:43:15,480 --> 01:43:17,983
I've brought you some pathetic children.

986
01:43:19,901 --> 01:43:23,405
You're not still upset
about that blasted dragon, are you?

987
01:43:27,075 --> 01:43:29,119
They took Norbert away.

988
01:43:29,536 --> 01:43:32,038
Dumbledore sent him to Romania...

989
01:43:32,247 --> 01:43:34,875
- ...to live in a colony.
- That's good, isn't it?

990
01:43:35,083 --> 01:43:38,879
- He'll be with his own kind.
- But what if he doesn't like Romania?

991
01:43:39,546 --> 01:43:42,174
What if the other dragons
are mean to him?

992
01:43:42,340 --> 01:43:46,928
- He's just a creature.
- For heaven's sake, cheer up.

993
01:43:47,137 --> 01:43:49,765
You're going into the forest,
after all.

994
01:43:49,973 --> 01:43:52,350
You need to stay alert.

995
01:43:52,517 --> 01:43:56,938
The forest? I thought that was
a joke. We can't go in there.

996
01:43:58,440 --> 01:44:02,360
No student can.
And there are...

997
01:44:04,070 --> 01:44:06,698
- ...werewolves.
- There's more than werewolves...

998
01:44:06,865 --> 01:44:10,577
...in those trees, boy.
You can be sure of that.

999
01:44:13,872 --> 01:44:15,207
Good evening.

1000
01:44:17,834 --> 01:44:19,377
Right.

1001
01:44:19,836 --> 01:44:21,379
Let's go.

1002
01:44:58,875 --> 01:45:03,046
- Hagrid, what's that?
- What we're here for.

1003
01:45:03,255 --> 01:45:07,509
See that?
It's unicorn blood.

1004
01:45:08,218 --> 01:45:10,762
I found one dead
a few weeks ago.

1005
01:45:11,221 --> 01:45:15,308
This one's been badly wounded
by someone.

1006
01:45:23,358 --> 01:45:26,987
So our job is...

1007
01:45:27,404 --> 01:45:29,239
...to find the poor creature.

1008
01:45:29,447 --> 01:45:32,450
Ron, Hermione, you two
come with me.

1009
01:45:32,826 --> 01:45:35,787
And Harry, you go with Malfoy.

1010
01:45:37,664 --> 01:45:41,209
- Fine. Then I'll take Fang.
- All right.

1011
01:45:41,543 --> 01:45:45,130
Just so you know,
he's a bloody coward.

1012
01:45:49,426 --> 01:45:53,388
Wait till my father hears about this.
This is servants' work.

1013
01:45:54,514 --> 01:45:58,560
If I didn't know better, Draco,
I'd say you were scared.

1014
01:45:58,768 --> 01:46:01,146
I'm not scared, Potter.

1015
01:46:02,480 --> 01:46:04,274
Did you hear that?

1016
01:46:06,818 --> 01:46:08,361
Come on, Fang.

1017
01:46:08,570 --> 01:46:10,155
Scared!

1018
01:46:35,055 --> 01:46:37,015
What's wrong, Fang?

1019
01:46:53,323 --> 01:46:55,408
Help!

1020
01:47:47,585 --> 01:47:53,258
Harry Potter, you must leave.
Many creatures here know you.

1021
01:47:53,466 --> 01:47:57,429
The forest isn't safe.
Especially for you.

1022
01:47:57,637 --> 01:48:00,265
What was that thing
you saved me from?

1023
01:48:00,432 --> 01:48:02,976
A monstrous creature.

1024
01:48:03,184 --> 01:48:05,979
It is a terrible crime
to kill a unicorn.

1025
01:48:06,187 --> 01:48:08,940
Drinking a unicorn's blood
will keep you alive...

1026
01:48:09,107 --> 01:48:11,776
...even if you're on the brink of death.

1027
01:48:11,985 --> 01:48:13,945
But at a terrible price.

1028
01:48:14,154 --> 01:48:17,073
For you have killed something so pure...

1029
01:48:17,282 --> 01:48:20,118
...that from the moment
the blood touches your lips...

1030
01:48:20,285 --> 01:48:24,122
...you will have a half-life,
a cursed life.

1031
01:48:24,330 --> 01:48:28,084
- Who would choose such a life?
- Can you think of no one?

1032
01:48:28,460 --> 01:48:30,587
Do you mean...

1033
01:48:30,795 --> 01:48:33,548
...that thing that killed the unicorn...

1034
01:48:33,757 --> 01:48:37,635
...that was drinking its blood...
was Voldemort?

1035
01:48:37,802 --> 01:48:41,556
Do you know what's hidden in the school
at this very moment, Mr. Potter?

1036
01:48:43,725 --> 01:48:46,144
The Sorcerer's Stone.

1037
01:48:46,686 --> 01:48:48,521
Harry!

1038
01:48:49,147 --> 01:48:53,193
Hello, Firenze. I see you've met
our young Mr. Potter.

1039
01:48:53,818 --> 01:48:55,904
Are you all right, Harry?

1040
01:48:57,238 --> 01:48:58,948
Harry Potter...

1041
01:48:59,157 --> 01:49:01,326
This is where I leave you.

1042
01:49:02,368 --> 01:49:06,247
You're safe now.
Good luck.

1043
01:49:13,797 --> 01:49:18,051
You mean You-Know-Who
is in the forest right now?

1044
01:49:18,259 --> 01:49:21,137
But he's weak.
He's surviving on unicorns.

1045
01:49:21,346 --> 01:49:24,182
Don't you see?
We had it all wrong.

1046
01:49:24,390 --> 01:49:28,728
Snape doesn't want the Stone for himself.
He wants it for Voldemort.

1047
01:49:28,937 --> 01:49:33,108
With the Elixir of Life,
Voldemort will regain his strength.

1048
01:49:33,691 --> 01:49:37,237
- And he'll come back.
- But if he comes back...

1049
01:49:37,445 --> 01:49:41,407
...you don't think he'll try
to kill you, do you?

1050
01:49:42,367 --> 01:49:45,036
I think he may have
tried to kill me today.

1051
01:49:46,246 --> 01:49:49,874
To think I've been worrying
about my Potions exam.

1052
01:49:50,083 --> 01:49:53,545
Wait a minute. There's something
we're forgetting.

1053
01:49:53,878 --> 01:49:58,091
Who's the one wizard
Voldemort has always feared?

1054
01:49:59,509 --> 01:50:00,969
Dumbledore.

1055
01:50:01,177 --> 01:50:04,722
As long as Dumbledore's here,
Harry, you're safe.

1056
01:50:04,931 --> 01:50:08,935
As long as Dumbledore's here,
no one can touch you.

1057
01:50:14,691 --> 01:50:18,153
They say the end-of-year exams
are very difficult.

1058
01:50:18,361 --> 01:50:23,825
- But I thought they were quite enjoyable.
- I didn't. Are you all right, Harry?

1059
01:50:24,242 --> 01:50:27,829
My scar. It keeps burning.

1060
01:50:28,163 --> 01:50:30,999
- It's happened before.
- Not like this.

1061
01:50:31,207 --> 01:50:34,085
- Go to the hospital wing.
- I think it's a warning...

1062
01:50:34,294 --> 01:50:35,920
...that danger is coming.

1063
01:50:43,595 --> 01:50:46,139
- Of course.
- What are you thinking?

1064
01:50:46,347 --> 01:50:50,101
Don't you think it's strange that what
Hagrid wanted most was a dragon...

1065
01:50:50,310 --> 01:50:52,770
...and a stranger just
happens to have one?

1066
01:50:52,979 --> 01:50:56,274
How many people do you meet
with dragon eggs?

1067
01:50:56,482 --> 01:50:58,693
How could I not have realized?

1068
01:51:04,199 --> 01:51:06,492
Who gave you
the dragon egg?

1069
01:51:06,701 --> 01:51:08,745
- What did he look like?
- I don't know.

1070
01:51:08,953 --> 01:51:10,788
I never saw his face.
He never took off his hood.

1071
01:51:10,955 --> 01:51:13,458
You must have talked
to this stranger.

1072
01:51:14,125 --> 01:51:17,795
He wanted to know what kind
of creatures I looked after.

1073
01:51:17,962 --> 01:51:22,091
I told him, "After Fluffy,
a dragon's nothing."

1074
01:51:22,300 --> 01:51:26,512
- Was he interested in Fluffy?
- Of course he was interested in Fluffy.

1075
01:51:26,971 --> 01:51:31,184
How often do you come across a
three-headed dog, even in the trade?

1076
01:51:31,392 --> 01:51:37,065
But I told him, "The trick with
beasts is knowing how to calm them."

1077
01:51:37,273 --> 01:51:41,402
Take Fluffy, for instance.
Play some music and he falls asleep.

1078
01:51:44,322 --> 01:51:46,616
I shouldn't have told you that.

1079
01:51:47,116 --> 01:51:49,077
Where are you going? Where...?

1080
01:51:56,251 --> 01:51:59,170
We need to see Professor
Dumbledore immediately!

1081
01:51:59,545 --> 01:52:01,673
I'm afraid Professor
Dumbledore isn't here.

1082
01:52:02,423 --> 01:52:05,593
He received an urgent owl
from the Ministry of Magic...

1083
01:52:05,802 --> 01:52:08,346
- ...and left for London.
- He's gone?

1084
01:52:08,513 --> 01:52:12,183
Now? But this is important.
It's about the Sorcerer's Stone!

1085
01:52:14,018 --> 01:52:16,437
- How do you know...?
- Someone's going to steal it!

1086
01:52:18,398 --> 01:52:21,025
I don't know how you found out
about the Stone, but I assure you...

1087
01:52:21,192 --> 01:52:23,778
...it's extremely well protected.

1088
01:52:23,987 --> 01:52:27,115
Now go back to your dormitories.
Quietly.

1089
01:52:36,374 --> 01:52:39,252
Hagrid wasn't talking to a stranger.
He was talking to Snape.

1090
01:52:39,460 --> 01:52:42,046
Which means he knows
how to get past Fluffy.

1091
01:52:42,255 --> 01:52:44,882
- And with Dumbledore gone...
- Good afternoon.

1092
01:52:48,219 --> 01:52:51,389
What could three young
Gryffindors like yourselves...

1093
01:52:51,597 --> 01:52:55,685
...be doing indoors,
on such a lovely day?

1094
01:53:00,606 --> 01:53:04,027
- We were just...
- You must be careful.

1095
01:53:04,736 --> 01:53:06,738
People will think you're...

1096
01:53:10,908 --> 01:53:13,619
...up to something.

1097
01:53:24,088 --> 01:53:26,132
What do we do now?

1098
01:53:26,341 --> 01:53:29,510
We go down the trapdoor.
Tonight.

1099
01:53:43,691 --> 01:53:45,401
Trevor.

1100
01:53:45,610 --> 01:53:48,780
Trevor! Go away,
you shouldn't be here!

1101
01:53:49,280 --> 01:53:51,282
Neither should you.

1102
01:53:52,450 --> 01:53:54,702
You're going out again, aren't you?

1103
01:53:54,911 --> 01:53:58,790
- Neville, listen. We were...
- I won't let you!

1104
01:53:58,998 --> 01:54:01,876
You'll get Gryffindor
into trouble again.

1105
01:54:02,460 --> 01:54:06,255
- I'll fight you.
- I'm really sorry.

1106
01:54:06,464 --> 01:54:08,132
<i>Petrificus Totalus.</i>

1107
01:54:16,057 --> 01:54:20,019
You scare me a little sometimes,
you know.

1108
01:54:20,228 --> 01:54:23,439
You're brilliant, but terrifying.

1109
01:54:24,565 --> 01:54:26,234
Let's go.

1110
01:54:26,651 --> 01:54:28,319
- Sorry.
- Sorry.

1111
01:54:28,486 --> 01:54:30,822
It's for your own good, you know.

1112
01:54:36,369 --> 01:54:38,329
You stepped on my foot!

1113
01:54:38,496 --> 01:54:40,248
Sorry.

1114
01:54:44,127 --> 01:54:46,087
<i>Alohomora.</i>

1115
01:54:58,224 --> 01:55:00,893
Wait a minute. It's...

1116
01:55:02,019 --> 01:55:04,188
...snoring.

1117
01:55:06,732 --> 01:55:09,152
Snape's already been here.

1118
01:55:09,694 --> 01:55:11,863
He enchanted the harp.

1119
01:55:12,738 --> 01:55:15,700
Ugh, what horrible breath.

1120
01:55:19,495 --> 01:55:21,539
- We have to move its paw.
- What?

1121
01:55:21,747 --> 01:55:23,541
Move it!

1122
01:55:27,128 --> 01:55:29,255
All right. Push!

1123
01:55:52,403 --> 01:55:56,157
I'll go first. Don't follow
until I give you the signal.

1124
01:55:56,365 --> 01:56:00,536
If anything goes wrong,
get out of here at once.

1125
01:56:02,079 --> 01:56:05,500
Isn't it a bit too quiet?

1126
01:56:06,250 --> 01:56:08,085
The harp.

1127
01:56:08,920 --> 01:56:10,880
It's stopped playing.

1128
01:56:21,849 --> 01:56:23,476
Jump!

1129
01:56:23,809 --> 01:56:25,603
Come on!

1130
01:56:36,739 --> 01:56:39,450
Lucky this plant
is here.

1131
01:56:54,966 --> 01:56:58,010
Stop moving.
This is Devil's Snare.

1132
01:56:58,219 --> 01:57:01,973
You have to relax.
Otherwise it'll kill you faster.

1133
01:57:02,139 --> 01:57:05,476
Kill us faster?
Oh, now I can relax!

1134
01:57:09,313 --> 01:57:10,648
Hermione!

1135
01:57:11,148 --> 01:57:14,277
- What are we going to do?
- Just relax!

1136
01:57:15,152 --> 01:57:19,699
- Hermione, where are you?
- Do as I say! Trust me!

1137
01:57:23,244 --> 01:57:24,245
Harry!

1138
01:57:24,996 --> 01:57:26,330
Harry!

1139
01:57:26,872 --> 01:57:29,000
- Are you all right?
- Yeah. Yeah, I'm fine.

1140
01:57:29,166 --> 01:57:32,086
- Help!
- He's not relaxing.

1141
01:57:32,295 --> 01:57:34,589
- Apparently not.
- We've got to do something!

1142
01:57:34,797 --> 01:57:36,173
What?

1143
01:57:36,382 --> 01:57:39,218
I remember reading
something in Herbology.

1144
01:57:39,427 --> 01:57:41,721
- Help!
- "Devil's Snare, Devil's Snare...

1145
01:57:41,929 --> 01:57:45,308
...it's deadly fun,
but hates the sun."

1146
01:57:45,516 --> 01:57:48,603
That's it! Devil's Snare
hates sunlight!

1147
01:57:48,811 --> 01:57:50,438
<i>Lumus Solem.</i>

1148
01:57:58,904 --> 01:58:01,407
- Ron, are you all right?
- Yeah.

1149
01:58:04,201 --> 01:58:06,287
Lucky we didn't panic.

1150
01:58:07,330 --> 01:58:10,458
Lucky Hermione pays
attention in Herbology.

1151
01:58:12,668 --> 01:58:15,838
- What's that?
- I don't know.

1152
01:58:16,589 --> 01:58:18,215
They look like wings.

1153
01:58:31,228 --> 01:58:34,690
How strange. I've never seen
birds like those.

1154
01:58:34,899 --> 01:58:38,069
They're not birds.
They're keys.

1155
01:58:38,736 --> 01:58:41,280
And I bet one of them
fits that door.

1156
01:58:45,576 --> 01:58:47,870
What's this about?

1157
01:58:48,079 --> 01:58:49,830
I don't know.

1158
01:58:56,087 --> 01:58:57,922
How strange.

1159
01:58:58,506 --> 01:59:00,466
<i>Alohomora!</i>

1160
01:59:03,678 --> 01:59:06,263
Well, it was worth a try.

1161
01:59:06,430 --> 01:59:09,642
What are we going to do?
There must be a thousand keys up there.

1162
01:59:09,850 --> 01:59:13,854
We're looking for a big, old one.
Maybe rusty.

1163
01:59:14,063 --> 01:59:17,274
There it is, I see it!
The one with the broken wing!

1164
01:59:20,903 --> 01:59:23,114
What's wrong, Harry?

1165
01:59:24,281 --> 01:59:27,618
- It's too simple.
- Come on, Harry!

1166
01:59:27,785 --> 01:59:30,621
If Snape could catch it with
that old broom, you can.

1167
01:59:30,871 --> 01:59:33,290
You're the youngest Seeker
in a century!

1168
01:59:51,225 --> 01:59:53,227
That complicates things a bit.

1169
02:00:15,499 --> 02:00:17,460
Grab the key!

1170
02:00:21,797 --> 02:00:23,507
Hurry up!

1171
02:00:56,207 --> 02:00:58,459
I don't like this.

1172
02:00:59,168 --> 02:01:02,755
- I don't like this one bit.
- Where are we?

1173
02:01:02,963 --> 02:01:06,884
- In a graveyard?
- This isn't a graveyard.

1174
02:01:14,683 --> 02:01:16,393
It's a chessboard.

1175
02:01:29,573 --> 02:01:31,534
There's the door!

1176
02:01:43,879 --> 02:01:46,799
- What do we do now?
- It's obvious, isn't it?

1177
02:01:47,007 --> 02:01:49,593
We have to play
to cross the room.

1178
02:01:50,261 --> 02:01:53,973
Harry, take the place
of that bishop.

1179
02:01:54,306 --> 02:01:57,935
Hermione, you'll be the rook
on the queen's side.

1180
02:01:58,769 --> 02:02:00,229
And as for me...

1181
02:02:00,604 --> 02:02:02,690
...I'll be a knight.

1182
02:02:09,905 --> 02:02:11,699
What happens now?

1183
02:02:12,491 --> 02:02:15,202
White moves first.

1184
02:02:15,744 --> 02:02:17,580
And then...

1185
02:02:19,290 --> 02:02:21,292
...we play.

1186
02:02:31,135 --> 02:02:32,469
Ron...

1187
02:02:32,761 --> 02:02:35,556
...you don't think this
is going to be like...

1188
02:02:36,432 --> 02:02:39,310
...real wizard's chess,
do you?

1189
02:02:40,269 --> 02:02:42,479
You there, to D5.

1190
02:02:57,995 --> 02:02:59,663
Yes, Hermione.

1191
02:02:59,872 --> 02:03:04,585
I think it's going to be exactly
like wizard's chess.

1192
02:03:10,633 --> 02:03:12,509
Rook to E4!

1193
02:03:16,847 --> 02:03:18,849
<i>Pawn to C6!</i>

1194
02:04:03,811 --> 02:04:05,938
Wait a minute.

1195
02:04:06,146 --> 02:04:07,898
That's right, Harry.

1196
02:04:08,107 --> 02:04:10,609
When I move forward...

1197
02:04:10,818 --> 02:04:12,820
...the queen will take me.

1198
02:04:13,404 --> 02:04:15,781
Then you can put
the king in checkmate.

1199
02:04:15,990 --> 02:04:18,617
- No. Ron, no!
- What is it?

1200
02:04:19,243 --> 02:04:22,287
- He's going to sacrifice himself.
- No, you can't!

1201
02:04:22,496 --> 02:04:24,081
There must be another way!

1202
02:04:24,289 --> 02:04:27,668
Do you want to stop Snape
from getting that Stone or not?

1203
02:04:28,127 --> 02:04:31,755
Harry, you have to
go on. I know it.

1204
02:04:32,214 --> 02:04:35,009
Not me. Not Hermione. You!

1205
02:04:45,269 --> 02:04:47,771
Knight to H3.

1206
02:05:09,084 --> 02:05:10,878
Check.

1207
02:05:40,157 --> 02:05:41,700
Ron!

1208
02:05:42,159 --> 02:05:44,203
No! Don't move!

1209
02:05:44,411 --> 02:05:47,372
Remember,
we're still playing.

1210
02:06:03,097 --> 02:06:04,431
Checkmate.

1211
02:06:24,243 --> 02:06:26,912
Take care of Ron.
Then go to the owlery...

1212
02:06:27,121 --> 02:06:30,541
...and send Dumbledore a message.
Ron's right.

1213
02:06:31,041 --> 02:06:33,043
I have to go on.

1214
02:06:33,460 --> 02:06:37,089
You'll be all right, Harry.
You're a great wizard.

1215
02:06:37,381 --> 02:06:39,383
You really are.

1216
02:06:39,800 --> 02:06:41,677
Not as good as you.

1217
02:06:42,886 --> 02:06:47,808
Me? Books and cleverness.
There are more important things.

1218
02:06:49,017 --> 02:06:51,687
Friendship and bravery.

1219
02:06:52,229 --> 02:06:54,731
And Harry, just be careful.

1220
02:07:32,561 --> 02:07:34,563
You?

1221
02:07:35,439 --> 02:07:39,151
No. It can't be.
Snape, he was the one who...

1222
02:07:39,359 --> 02:07:42,321
Yes, he seemed the obvious choice,
didn't he?

1223
02:07:42,529 --> 02:07:44,615
With him around,
who would suspect...

1224
02:07:44,781 --> 02:07:48,785
...poor, st-stuttering
Professor Quirrell?

1225
02:07:49,411 --> 02:07:55,459
But that day during the Quidditch match,
Snape tried to kill me.

1226
02:07:55,626 --> 02:07:58,378
No, boy.
I tried to kill you.

1227
02:07:58,837 --> 02:08:03,133
And if Snape's cloak hadn't
caught fire and distracted me...

1228
02:08:03,300 --> 02:08:05,552
...I would have killed you.

1229
02:08:05,761 --> 02:08:08,680
Despite Snape's little
countercurse.

1230
02:08:09,014 --> 02:08:11,183
Snape was trying to save me?

1231
02:08:11,391 --> 02:08:15,520
I knew you were a threat to me,
especially after Halloween.

1232
02:08:16,563 --> 02:08:21,151
- So you let the troll in?
- Very good, Potter. Yes.

1233
02:08:21,360 --> 02:08:24,321
Unfortunately,
I didn't fool Snape.

1234
02:08:24,905 --> 02:08:28,742
While everyone ran to the dungeon,
he went to stop me on the third floor.

1235
02:08:30,661 --> 02:08:34,331
Of course,
he never trusted me again.

1236
02:08:35,249 --> 02:08:37,501
He rarely left me alone.

1237
02:08:37,834 --> 02:08:39,878
But he doesn't understand.

1238
02:08:40,712 --> 02:08:44,007
I'm never alone. Never.

1239
02:08:44,967 --> 02:08:48,512
Now... what does this mirror do?

1240
02:08:50,597 --> 02:08:52,766
I see what I desire.

1241
02:08:53,267 --> 02:08:56,144
I see myself holding the Stone.

1242
02:08:56,353 --> 02:09:00,065
- But how do I get it?
- Use the boy.

1243
02:09:00,857 --> 02:09:03,026
Come here, Potter!

1244
02:09:03,193 --> 02:09:05,028
Right now!

1245
02:09:16,873 --> 02:09:20,335
Tell me... what do you see?

1246
02:09:46,028 --> 02:09:48,238
What is it? What do you see?

1247
02:09:48,739 --> 02:09:51,241
I'm shaking hands with Dumbledore.

1248
02:09:52,367 --> 02:09:55,662
- I've won the House Cup.
- He's lying.

1249
02:09:56,079 --> 02:09:59,833
Tell the truth!
What do you see?

1250
02:10:00,042 --> 02:10:04,463
- Let me speak to him.
- Master, you're not strong enough.

1251
02:10:04,671 --> 02:10:08,592
I have enough strength for this.

1252
02:10:26,860 --> 02:10:29,821
Harry Potter...

1253
02:10:30,030 --> 02:10:32,491
...we meet again.

1254
02:10:32,783 --> 02:10:35,535
- Voldemort.
- Yes.

1255
02:10:35,744 --> 02:10:38,121
You see what
I've become?

1256
02:10:38,372 --> 02:10:42,125
You see what I have
to do to survive?

1257
02:10:42,292 --> 02:10:46,213
Sharing another's body,
like a mere parasite.

1258
02:10:46,963 --> 02:10:50,300
Unicorn blood
can sustain me...

1259
02:10:50,509 --> 02:10:53,512
...but it cannot give me
a body of my own.

1260
02:10:54,346 --> 02:10:57,057
But there is something that can.

1261
02:10:58,141 --> 02:11:03,355
Something you conveniently
have in your pocket.

1262
02:11:04,147 --> 02:11:05,524
Stop him!

1263
02:11:10,779 --> 02:11:12,823
Don't be a fool.

1264
02:11:13,657 --> 02:11:16,493
Why suffer a horrible death...

1265
02:11:17,285 --> 02:11:22,332
- ...when you can join me and live?
- Never!

1266
02:11:24,167 --> 02:11:25,961
Bravery.

1267
02:11:26,503 --> 02:11:28,922
Your parents had it too.

1268
02:11:29,840 --> 02:11:33,176
Tell me, Harry...

1269
02:11:33,343 --> 02:11:37,264
...would you like to see
your mother and father again?

1270
02:11:37,472 --> 02:11:39,141
Together...

1271
02:11:39,683 --> 02:11:42,102
...we can bring them back.

1272
02:11:42,686 --> 02:11:46,731
All I ask for
is one thing in return.

1273
02:11:54,156 --> 02:11:57,117
That's it, Harry.

1274
02:11:58,243 --> 02:12:01,538
There is no good and evil.

1275
02:12:02,330 --> 02:12:05,292
There is only power...

1276
02:12:05,500 --> 02:12:09,004
...and those too weak
to seek it.

1277
02:12:10,380 --> 02:12:11,882
Together...

1278
02:12:12,048 --> 02:12:15,302
...we'll do extraordinary things.

1279
02:12:15,760 --> 02:12:18,054
Just give me the Stone!

1280
02:12:20,682 --> 02:12:23,101
- Liar!
- Kill him!

1281
02:12:47,667 --> 02:12:51,505
- What magic is this?
- Fool! Get the Stone!

1282
02:14:38,236 --> 02:14:40,530
Good afternoon, Harry.

1283
02:14:42,907 --> 02:14:47,370
- Gifts from your admirers?
- Admirers?

1284
02:14:47,579 --> 02:14:51,541
What happened in the dungeons
between you and Professor Quirrell...

1285
02:14:51,750 --> 02:14:53,752
...is completely secret.

1286
02:14:53,960 --> 02:14:57,255
So, naturally, the whole school knows.

1287
02:15:01,718 --> 02:15:04,721
I see your friend Ronald
has spared you the trouble...

1288
02:15:04,888 --> 02:15:09,934
- ...of opening your Chocolate Frogs.
- Ron came? Is he all right?

1289
02:15:10,143 --> 02:15:12,312
- How's Hermione?
- Fine.

1290
02:15:13,021 --> 02:15:15,440
They're both perfectly well.

1291
02:15:16,441 --> 02:15:19,319
- What happened to the Stone?
- Calm down, my dear boy.

1292
02:15:19,611 --> 02:15:22,155
The Stone has been destroyed.

1293
02:15:22,989 --> 02:15:25,742
My friend Nicolas and I
had a little talk...

1294
02:15:25,909 --> 02:15:30,413
...and agreed it was
for the best.

1295
02:15:31,331 --> 02:15:34,834
But then Flamel
is going to die, isn't he?

1296
02:15:37,253 --> 02:15:41,633
He has enough Elixir
to put his affairs in order.

1297
02:15:42,884 --> 02:15:46,429
But yes... he will die.

1298
02:15:46,638 --> 02:15:48,807
How did I get the Stone?

1299
02:15:49,015 --> 02:15:51,685
One minute, I was looking
in the mirror, and the next...

1300
02:15:51,893 --> 02:15:55,105
You see, only a person...

1301
02:15:56,022 --> 02:15:58,608
...who wanted to find the Stone...

1302
02:15:58,817 --> 02:16:01,820
...find it, but not use it...

1303
02:16:02,028 --> 02:16:04,489
...could obtain it.

1304
02:16:05,782 --> 02:16:09,494
That was one of my
more brilliant ideas.

1305
02:16:09,703 --> 02:16:13,123
And between you and me,
that's saying something.

1306
02:16:15,959 --> 02:16:19,045
Does that mean,
now that the Stone is gone...

1307
02:16:19,254 --> 02:16:21,798
...Voldemort can never come back?

1308
02:16:22,048 --> 02:16:23,967
I'm afraid...

1309
02:16:25,176 --> 02:16:28,555
...there are ways he can return.

1310
02:16:29,973 --> 02:16:36,146
Harry, do you know why Professor
Quirrell couldn't bear your touch?

1311
02:16:36,896 --> 02:16:41,651
Because of your mother.
She sacrificed herself for you.

1312
02:16:42,110 --> 02:16:44,571
And that kind of act
leaves a mark.

1313
02:16:45,530 --> 02:16:49,242
No. That kind of mark
cannot be seen.

1314
02:16:49,534 --> 02:16:52,203
It lives in your very skin.

1315
02:16:52,787 --> 02:16:54,497
What is it?

1316
02:16:55,248 --> 02:16:59,127
Love, Harry. Love.

1317
02:17:05,842 --> 02:17:10,764
Ah, Bertie Bott's
Every Flavor Beans.

1318
02:17:11,431 --> 02:17:15,643
I was unfortunate enough
to come across a vomit-flavored one.

1319
02:17:16,352 --> 02:17:19,606
And since then, I'm afraid
I've rather lost my liking for them.

1320
02:17:19,939 --> 02:17:22,567
But I don't think I'm
taking much of a risk...

1321
02:17:23,485 --> 02:17:25,528
...with a toffee one.

1322
02:17:29,866 --> 02:17:31,326
Alas.

1323
02:17:32,160 --> 02:17:33,995
Earwax.

1324
02:17:49,552 --> 02:17:52,722
- Are you all right, Ron?
- Fine. You?

1325
02:17:53,848 --> 02:17:56,476
I'm fine. Hermione?

1326
02:17:57,227 --> 02:17:59,062
Never better.

1327
02:18:14,828 --> 02:18:17,330
Another year has gone by.

1328
02:18:18,122 --> 02:18:20,083
And now, as I understand it...

1329
02:18:20,250 --> 02:18:22,418
...it's time to award the House Cup.

1330
02:18:22,585 --> 02:18:25,463
The points stand as follows:

1331
02:18:25,713 --> 02:18:30,093
In fourth place, Gryffindor
with 312 points.

1332
02:18:33,429 --> 02:18:35,265
In third place:

1333
02:18:35,473 --> 02:18:39,102
Hufflepuff with 352 points.

1334
02:18:44,274 --> 02:18:46,192
In second place:

1335
02:18:46,401 --> 02:18:51,155
Ravenclaw with 426 points.

1336
02:18:57,078 --> 02:19:01,791
And in first place, with 472 points...

1337
02:19:02,000 --> 02:19:05,503
- ...Slytherin House.
- Well done.

1338
02:19:15,930 --> 02:19:20,018
Yes, yes, congratulations, Slytherin.
However...

1339
02:19:20,310 --> 02:19:24,188
...we must take into account
recent events.

1340
02:19:24,689 --> 02:19:29,110
And I have a few last-minute
points to award.

1341
02:19:30,361 --> 02:19:33,406
To Miss Hermione Granger...

1342
02:19:33,615 --> 02:19:35,992
...for the cool use of intellect...

1343
02:19:36,200 --> 02:19:38,912
...while others were
in grave danger...

1344
02:19:39,579 --> 02:19:41,623
...fifty points.

1345
02:19:51,841 --> 02:19:55,011
Second, to Mr. Ronald Weasley...

1346
02:19:55,929 --> 02:20:01,976
...for the best-played game of chess
Hogwarts has seen in years...

1347
02:20:02,644 --> 02:20:04,687
...fifty points.

1348
02:20:08,191 --> 02:20:10,026
And third...

1349
02:20:10,777 --> 02:20:12,904
...to Mr. Harry Potter...

1350
02:20:13,821 --> 02:20:18,201
...for sheer nerve and outstanding courage...

1351
02:20:18,701 --> 02:20:23,706
...I award Gryffindor House
sixty points.

1352
02:20:31,923 --> 02:20:35,718
- We're tied with Slytherin!
- And finally...

1353
02:20:35,927 --> 02:20:40,223
...it takes a great deal of courage
to stand up to our enemies...

1354
02:20:40,390 --> 02:20:43,810
...but a great deal more
to stand up to our friends.

1355
02:20:44,352 --> 02:20:47,438
I award ten points...

1356
02:20:47,647 --> 02:20:50,233
...to Neville Longbottom.

1357
02:21:04,080 --> 02:21:06,416
Assuming my
calculations are correct...

1358
02:21:06,582 --> 02:21:11,254
...I believe a change
of decoration is in order.

1359
02:21:17,260 --> 02:21:20,638
Gryffindor wins the House Cup.

1360
02:21:22,765 --> 02:21:25,018
Hooray! Hooray!

1361
02:21:39,157 --> 02:21:41,576
We won!

1362
02:21:58,801 --> 02:22:01,429
Come on, hurry up, you'll be late.

1363
02:22:02,263 --> 02:22:05,600
The train's leaving. Get going, get going.
Come on, hurry.

1364
02:22:11,939 --> 02:22:14,942
- Come on, Harry.
- Just a minute.

1365
02:22:21,657 --> 02:22:24,494
Didn't think you were going
without saying goodbye, did you?

1366
02:22:28,706 --> 02:22:30,625
This is for you.

1367
02:22:47,016 --> 02:22:49,143
Thank you, Hagrid.

1368
02:22:55,066 --> 02:22:59,529
Now go on. Off you go.
And listen, Harry...

1369
02:22:59,904 --> 02:23:02,365
...if that awful cousin of yours, Dudley...

1370
02:23:02,532 --> 02:23:06,202
...gives you any trouble, you can always...

1371
02:23:06,494 --> 02:23:10,540
...threaten to give him a pair
of ears to match his tail.

1372
02:23:10,748 --> 02:23:15,711
But we're not allowed to use magic
outside Hogwarts. You know that.

1373
02:23:16,087 --> 02:23:17,672
Yes, I know.

1374
02:23:17,880 --> 02:23:20,550
But your cousin doesn't, does he?

1375
02:23:26,055 --> 02:23:29,225
Feels strange going home, doesn't it?

1376
02:23:29,433 --> 02:23:33,563
I'm not going home.
Not really.
